CC.provideCourse.bind(null,"math")({"lessons":{"math-01":{"html":"<p>Before solving equations, mathematics gives us a language for grouping objects (<strong>sets</strong>) and naming the kinds of numbers we work with (<strong>number systems</strong>).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-sets-and-set-operations\"><h2 id=\"sets-and-set-operations\">Sets and set operations</h2>\n<p>A <strong>set</strong> is a well-defined collection of distinct elements, written inside curly braces, such as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}\"></span>.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Element</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\in A\"></span> (\"2 is in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>\"), <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9 \\notin A\"></span> (\"9 is not in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>\").</li><li><strong>Empty set</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{\\}\"></span> (0 elements).</li><li><strong>Subset</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\subseteq B\"></span> means every element of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> is also in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>. A set with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> elements has <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^n\"></span> subsets.</li></ul>\n<p>Suppose <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"U = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B = \\{3, 4, 5\\}\"></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Union</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cup B\"></span></td><td>In <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> <strong>or</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span> (or both)</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Intersection</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B\"></span></td><td>In <strong>both</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{3, 4\\}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Difference</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\setminus B\"></span></td><td>In <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> <strong>but not</strong> in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 2\\}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Complement</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A&#x27;\"></span></td><td>In universal set <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"U\"></span> <strong>but not</strong> in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{5, 6\\}\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Counting formula (Inclusion–Exclusion)</strong>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = s(A) + s(B) - s(A \\cap B)\"></span><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\" *(In Turkish math exams, \"></span>s(A)<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\" denotes the number of elements in set \"></span>A$.)*</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-number-sets-mathbb-n-subset-mathbb-z-subset-mathbb-q-subset-mathbb-r\"><h2 id=\"number-sets-mathbb-n-subset-mathbb-z-subset-mathbb-q-subset-mathbb-r\">Number sets (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N} \\subset \\mathbb{Z} \\subset \\mathbb{Q} \\subset \\mathbb{R}\"></span>)</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Natural numbers (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N}\"></span>)</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{0, 1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}\"></span> (Positive integers <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Z}^+ = \\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}\"></span>).</li><li><strong>Integers (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Z}\"></span>)</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{\\dots, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, \\dots\\}\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Rational numbers (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Q}\"></span>)</strong>: fractions <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{a}{b}\"></span> where <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b \\ne 0\"></span> (includes terminating and repeating decimals).</li><li><strong>Irrational numbers (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Q}&#x27;\"></span>)</strong>: decimals that never terminate and never repeat (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{2}, \\pi, e\"></span>).</li><li><strong>Real numbers (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span>)</strong>: all rational and irrational numbers together.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice set operations and counting problems with the interactive drill:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"sets\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting to subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B)\"></span> when finding <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B)\"></span>—elements in both sets get counted twice otherwise!</li><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is a positive integer. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is an <strong>even integer</strong> and a <strong>natural number</strong> in Turkish curriculum (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N}\"></span>), but it is <strong>neither positive nor negative</strong>.</li><li>Confusing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\setminus B\"></span> with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B \\setminus A\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1,2,3\\} \\setminus \\{3,4\\} = \\{1,2\\}\"></span>, whereas <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{3,4\\} \\setminus \\{1,2,3\\} = \\{4\\}\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>set</strong></td><td>a well-defined collection of distinct elements</td><td lang=\"tr\">küme</td></tr><tr><td><strong>union (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cup B\"></span>)</strong></td><td>elements belonging to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>, or both</td><td lang=\"tr\">birleşim</td></tr><tr><td><strong>intersection (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B\"></span>)</strong></td><td>elements belonging to both <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">kesişim</td></tr><tr><td><strong>rational number (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Q}\"></span>)</strong></td><td>any number expressible as a fraction <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a/b\"></span> with integers <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a, b \\ne 0\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">rasyonel sayı</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A) = 12\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(B) = 9\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B) = 4\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"21","why":"forgot to subtract the overlap <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B)\"></span>"},{"h":"17","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 + 9 - 4 = 17\"></span>"},{"h":"15","why":"subtracted too much"},{"h":"25","why":"added the intersection instead of subtracting"}],"why":"By inclusion–exclusion, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = 12 + 9 - 4 = 17\"></span>."},{"q":"How many subsets does the set <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"K = \\{a, b, c, d\\}\"></span> have?","opts":[{"h":"4","why":"4 is the number of elements, not subsets"},{"h":"8","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 = 8\"></span> is for 3 elements"},{"h":"16","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^4 = 16\"></span> subsets (including <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"K\"></span> itself)"},{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 3\"></span> is not the subset formula"}],"why":"A set with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> elements has <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^n\"></span> subsets; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^4 = 16\"></span>."},{"q":"Which number is <strong>irrational</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\notin \\mathbb{Q}\"></span>)?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-7\"></span>","why":"integer, so rational (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-7/1\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.25\"></span>","why":"terminating decimal (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1/4\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{9}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{9} = 3\"></span>, which is an integer"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span> is not a perfect square, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5}\"></span> never terminates or repeats"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5}\"></span> cannot be written as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a/b\"></span> with integers."}]],"id":"math-01","title":"Sets and number systems","goal":"perform set operations (union, intersection, difference, complement) and classify numbers into natural, integer, rational, and real sets","week":"1","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"set","m":"a well-defined collection of distinct elements","tr":"küme"},{"t":"union ($A \\cup B$)","m":"elements belonging to $A$, $B$, or both","tr":"birleşim"},{"t":"intersection ($A \\cap B$)","m":"elements belonging to both $A$ and $B$","tr":"kesişim"},{"t":"rational number ($\\mathbb{Q}$)","m":"any number expressible as a fraction $a/b$ with integers $a, b \\ne 0$","tr":"rasyonel sayı"}]},"math-02":{"html":"<p>Fractions appear inside almost every algebra, ratio, and equation problem. Mastering fraction arithmetic and order of operations saves easy points on midterms.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-fraction-rules-concrete-examples-first\"><h2 id=\"fraction-rules-concrete-examples-first\">Fraction rules (concrete examples first)</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Simplify first</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{12}{18} = \\frac{12 \\div 6}{18 \\div 6} = \\frac{2}{3}\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Add / Subtract</strong> (common denominator): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{8}{12} + \\frac{3}{12} = \\frac{11}{12}\"></span>$</li><li><strong>Multiply</strong> (top × top, bottom × bottom — cancel diagonally first!): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{8}{9} = \\frac{1}{1} \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}\"></span>$</li><li><strong>Divide</strong> (\"keep, change, flip\"): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{6} \\div \\frac{10}{3} = \\frac{5}{6} \\times \\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{1}{4}\"></span>$</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-order-of-operations-pemdas-i-lem-nceli-i\"><h2 id=\"order-of-operations-pemdas-i-lem-nceli-i\">Order of operations (PEMDAS / İşlem Önceliği)</h2>\n<ol><li><strong>Parentheses</strong> <code>(...)</code> (innermost first)</li><li><strong>Exponents / Radicals</strong></li><li><strong>Multiplication &amp; Division</strong> (left to right)</li><li><strong>Addition &amp; Subtraction</strong> (left to right)</li></ol>\n<p>Example: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 3 \\times (4 - 1)^2 = 2 + 3 \\times 9 = 2 + 27 = 29\"></span> (never add <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2+3\"></span> before multiplying!).</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-repeating-decimals-to-fractions\"><h2 id=\"repeating-decimals-to-fractions\">Repeating decimals to fractions</h2>\n<p>Shortcut formula for repeating decimals (devirli ondalık sayılar): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\text{Value} = \\frac{\\text{all digits} - \\text{non-repeating digits}}{9\\text{s for repeating digits, then }0\\text{s for decimal non-repeating digits}}\"></span>$</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{7} = \\frac{7}{9}\"></span></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1.2\\overline{3} = \\frac{123 - 12}{90} = \\frac{111}{90} = \\frac{37}{30}\"></span></li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice fraction and decimal operations with the interactive drill:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"fractions\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Adding denominators when adding fractions: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}\"></span> is <strong>not</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{5}\"></span>; it is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}\"></span>.</li><li>Canceling across addition: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2 + x}{2}\"></span> is <strong>not</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + x\"></span>! It equals <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + \\frac{x}{2}\"></span>. You can only cancel common <strong>factors</strong> (multiplication).</li><li>Dividing by zero: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{0}\"></span> is <strong>undefined</strong> (while <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{0}{5} = 0\"></span>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>numerator</strong></td><td>the top number of a fraction</td><td lang=\"tr\">pay</td></tr><tr><td><strong>denominator</strong></td><td>the bottom number of a fraction (must not be zero)</td><td lang=\"tr\">payda</td></tr><tr><td><strong>reciprocal</strong></td><td>the flipped fraction <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b/a\"></span> of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a/b\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">çarpmaya göre tersi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>repeating decimal</strong></td><td>a decimal whose digits repeat endlessly (e.g., <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{3} = 1/3\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">devirli ondalık sayı</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Compute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{1}{6}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{2}\"></span>","why":"cannot subtract numerators and denominators directly"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{7}{12}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"common denominator 12: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{12} - \\frac{2}{12} = \\frac{7}{12}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{12}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9-4}{12}\"></span> would be wrong (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{2}{12}\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{12}\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3-1}{4}\"></span> ignores the 6"}],"why":"Common denominator is 12: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{12} - \\frac{2}{12} = \\frac{7}{12}\"></span>."},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{4} + 0.\\overline{5}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.9\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4/9 + 5/9 = 9/9 = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{5}{9} = \\frac{9}{9} = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{10}\"></span>","why":"repeating over 9, not 10"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{5}\"></span>","why":"incorrect conversion"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{4} = \\frac{4}{9}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{5} = \\frac{5}{9}\"></span>, summing to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{9} = 1\"></span>."},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} \\div \\frac{4}{9}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{8}{27}\"></span>","why":"multiplied without flipping the second fraction"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{18}{12} = \\frac{3}{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","why":"forgot to invert"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{6}{12}\"></span>","why":"equals <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1/2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3/2\"></span>"}],"why":"Keep <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>, change <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\div\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\times\"></span>, flip <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{9}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{4}\"></span> → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-02","title":"Rational numbers, fractions, and decimals","goal":"add, subtract, multiply, and divide fractions cleanly and convert repeating decimals into fractions","week":"2","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"numerator","m":"the top number of a fraction","tr":"pay"},{"t":"denominator","m":"the bottom number of a fraction (must not be zero)","tr":"payda"},{"t":"reciprocal","m":"the flipped fraction $b/a$ of $a/b$","tr":"çarpmaya göre tersi"},{"t":"repeating decimal","m":"a decimal whose digits repeat endlessly (e.g., $0.\\overline{3} = 1/3$)","tr":"devirli ondalık sayı"}]},"math-03":{"html":"<p>Two classic Turkish university math topics are <strong>digit/place-value puzzles</strong> (basamak kavramı) and <strong>divisibility rules</strong> (bölünebilme kuralları).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-place-value-basamak-kavram\"><h2 id=\"place-value-basamak-kavram\">Place value (Basamak kavramı)</h2>\n<p>A two-digit number <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab}\"></span> means <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10a + b\"></span> (with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\in \\{1..9\\}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b \\in \\{0..9\\}\"></span>). A three-digit number <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{abc}\"></span> means <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100a + 10b + c\"></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab} + \\overline{ba} = 99\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span>? $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(10a + b) + (10b + a) = 11a + 11b = 11(a + b) = 99 \\implies a + b = 9\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-divisibility-rules-with-remainders\"><h2 id=\"divisibility-rules-with-remainders\">Divisibility rules (with remainders!)</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Divisor</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Last digit is even (<code>0, 2, 4, 6, 8</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td><strong>Sum of digits</strong> is divisible by 3 (and remainder mod 3 equals digit-sum mod 3!)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td><strong>Last 2 digits</strong> form a number divisible by 4</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Last digit is <code>0</code> or <code>5</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td><strong>Last 3 digits</strong> form a number divisible by 8</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td><strong>Sum of digits</strong> is divisible by 9</td></tr><tr><td><strong>10</strong></td><td>Last digit is <code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>11</strong></td><td>Alternating sum from right (<code>+ - + - ...</code>) is divisible by 11</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Combined rules</strong>: Divisible by <strong>6</strong> = divisible by 2 <strong>and</strong> 3. Divisible by <strong>12</strong> = 3 <strong>and</strong> 4. Divisible by <strong>15</strong> = 3 <strong>and</strong> 5. (Always split into <strong>coprime</strong> factors!)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: Find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> if the 4-digit number <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"354a\"></span> is divisible by <strong>6</strong>.</p>\n<ul><li>Divisible by 2 → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\in \\{0, 2, 4, 6, 8\\}\"></span>.</li><li>Divisible by 3 → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 + 5 + 4 + a = 12 + a\"></span> is a multiple of 3 → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\in \\{0, 3, 6, 9\\}\"></span>.</li><li>Both true → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\in \\{0, 6\\}\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice divisibility and remainder problems below:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"divisibility\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Checking divisibility by <strong>12</strong> using 2 and 6 instead of <strong>3 and 4</strong>. You must pick <strong>coprime</strong> factors (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(3,4)=1\"></span>); for example, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18\"></span> is divisible by 2 and 6, yet NOT divisible by 12!</li><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab}\"></span> means <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\times b\"></span> in digit problems. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab}\"></span> with a bar/digits means <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10a + b\"></span>.</li><li>Forgetting that the leading digit <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> of a multi-digit number <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{abc}\"></span> cannot be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>place value</strong></td><td>the value of a digit based on its position (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1, 10, 100, \\dots\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">basamak değeri</td></tr><tr><td><strong>divisibility</strong></td><td>when one integer divides another with remainder 0</td><td lang=\"tr\">bölünebilme</td></tr><tr><td><strong>coprime</strong></td><td>two integers whose greatest common divisor is 1</td><td lang=\"tr\">aralarında asal</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"What is the remainder when <code>4527</code> is divided by <strong>9</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"0","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+5+2+7 = 18\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18\"></span> is divisible by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span>, so the remainder is 0"},{"h":"2","why":"sum of digits is 18, not 20"},{"h":"4","why":"sum of digits is 18, not 22"},{"h":"7","why":"7 is only the units digit (that applies to mod 10, not mod 9)"}],"why":"For divisibility by 9, the remainder equals the digit sum mod 9: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+5+2+7 = 18 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 9\"></span>."},{"q":"Which digit <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> makes the 4-digit number <code>243a</code> divisible by <strong>4</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"<code>30</code> is not divisible by 4"},{"h":"2","ok":1,"why":"<code>32</code> is divisible by 4 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 8 = 32\"></span>)"},{"h":"4","why":"<code>34</code> is not divisible by 4"},{"h":"8","why":"<code>38</code> is not divisible by 4"}],"why":"A number is divisible by 4 if its last two digits (<code>3a</code>) are divisible by 4 (<code>32</code> and <code>36</code>)."},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab} - \\overline{ba} = 36\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a - b\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9(a-b) = 36 \\implies a - b = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"4","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(10a+b) - (10b+a) = 9(a-b) = 36 \\implies a - b = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9 \\times 6 = 54 \\ne 36\"></span>"},{"h":"9","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9 \\times 9 = 81 \\ne 36\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab} - \\overline{ba} = 9(a - b)\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"36 \\div 9 = 4\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-03","title":"Place value, digits, and divisibility rules","goal":"expand multi-digit numbers using place value and apply divisibility rules for 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, and 11","week":"3","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"place value","m":"the value of a digit based on its position ($1, 10, 100, \\dots$)","tr":"basamak değeri"},{"t":"divisibility","m":"when one integer divides another with remainder 0","tr":"bölünebilme"},{"t":"coprime","m":"two integers whose greatest common divisor is 1","tr":"aralarında asal"}]},"math-04":{"html":"<p>In Computer Programming, you constantly use <strong>base 2 (binary)</strong>, <strong>base 8 (octal)</strong>, <strong>base 16 (hex)</strong>, and the <code>%</code> (<strong>modulo</strong>) operator. Here is the math behind them.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-number-bases-taban-aritmeti-i\"><h2 id=\"number-bases-taban-aritmeti-i\">Number bases (Taban aritmetiği)</h2>\n<p>In <strong>base <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span></strong>, digits range from <code>0</code> to <code>b - 1</code>, and places are powers of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b^0, b^1, b^2, \\dots\"></span>).</p>\n<h3>Base <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span> → Base 10 (expand by powers of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span>)</h3>\n<div class=\"math display\" data-tex=\"(231)_4 = 2 \\cdot 4^2 + 3 \\cdot 4^1 + 1 \\cdot 4^0 = 32 + 12 + 1 = 45_{10}\"></div>\n<h3>Base 10 → Base <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span> (repeated division, read remainders bottom-up!)</h3>\n<p>Convert <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25_{10}\"></span> to base 2:</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25 \\div 2 = 12\"></span> R <strong><code>1</code></strong></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 \\div 2 = 6\"></span> R <strong><code>0</code></strong></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\div 2 = 3\"></span> R <strong><code>0</code></strong></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\div 2 = 1\"></span> R <strong><code>1</code></strong></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 \\div 2 = 0\"></span> R <strong><code>1</code></strong></li></ul>\n<p>Read remainders bottom-up: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(11001)_2\"></span>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-modular-arithmetic-bmod-n\"><h2 id=\"modular-arithmetic-bmod-n\">Modular arithmetic (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\bmod n\"></span>)</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\equiv r \\pmod n\"></span> means <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"r\"></span> leave the <strong>same remainder</strong> when divided by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n &gt; 1\"></span>).</p>\n<ul><li>Example: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"17 \\equiv 2 \\pmod 5\"></span> because <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"17 = 3 \\times 5 + 2\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Clock / cycle problems</strong>: What day is 100 days after Monday? <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100 \\div 7 = 14\"></span> R <strong>2</strong> → 2 days after Monday = <strong>Wednesday</strong>.</li><li><strong>Shortcut for large powers</strong>: Reduce the base mod <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> first, or find the repeating cycle! - Find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{10} \\pmod 7\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 = 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 7\"></span>. So <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{10} = (2^3)^3 \\cdot 2^1 \\equiv 1^3 \\cdot 2 = 2 \\pmod 7\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice both number bases and modular arithmetic:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"bases\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"modular\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Reading the division remainders <strong>top-down</strong> instead of <strong>bottom-up</strong> when converting from base 10 to base <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span>.</li><li>Writing a digit <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge b\"></span> inside a base-<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span> number (for example, <code>(142)_4</code> is invalid because base 4 only allows digits <code>0, 1, 2, 3</code>).</li><li>Forgetting that remainders in modular arithmetic are always chosen in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 \\le r &lt; n\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>base (radix)</strong></td><td>the number of unique digits in a positional number system (e.g., 2, 10, 16)</td><td lang=\"tr\">sayı tabanı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>modulo (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\bmod\"></span>)</strong></td><td>operation giving the remainder after integer division</td><td lang=\"tr\">modüler aritmetik (mod)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>congruent (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\equiv b \\pmod n\"></span>)</strong></td><td>having the same remainder when divided by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">denktir</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Convert <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(10110)_2\"></span> to base 10:","opts":[{"h":"18","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 2 = 18\"></span> (missed the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span> bit)"},{"h":"22","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\\cdot 16 + 0\\cdot 8 + 1\\cdot 4 + 1\\cdot 2 + 0\\cdot 1 = 22\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8\"></span>"},{"h":"26","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8 + 2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(10110)_2 = 16 + 4 + 2 = 22\"></span>."},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(34)_{5}\"></span> in base 10?","opts":[{"h":"14","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\cdot 5 + 4 = 19\"></span>, not 14"},{"h":"19","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0 = 15 + 4 = 19\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\cdot 5 + 4\"></span>"},{"h":"34","why":"that would be base 10"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(34)_5 = 3 \\times 5 + 4 = 19\"></span>."},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{100} \\pmod 4\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"3 and 4 are coprime, so remainder is never 0"},{"h":"1","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\equiv -1 \\pmod 4\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-1)^{100} = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"2","why":"powers of 3 are odd, never <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\equiv 2 \\pmod 4\"></span>"},{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^1 \\equiv 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^2 = 9 \\equiv 1\"></span>; even exponent gives 1"}],"why":"Since <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\equiv -1 \\pmod 4\"></span>, any even power <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{100} \\equiv (-1)^{100} = 1 \\pmod 4\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-04","title":"Number bases and modular arithmetic","goal":"convert integers between base 10 and other bases (2, 8, 16) and compute remainders in modular arithmetic","week":"3","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"base (radix)","m":"the number of unique digits in a positional number system (e.g., 2, 10, 16)","tr":"sayı tabanı"},{"t":"modulo ($\\bmod$)","m":"operation giving the remainder after integer division","tr":"modüler aritmetik (mod)"},{"t":"congruent ($a \\equiv b \\pmod n$)","m":"having the same remainder when divided by $n$","tr":"denktir"}]},"math-05":{"html":"<p>Prime numbers are the building blocks of all integers—and <strong>GCD</strong> and <strong>LCM</strong> show up in fraction arithmetic, scheduling problems, and cryptography.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-prime-numbers-and-factorization\"><h2 id=\"prime-numbers-and-factorization\">Prime numbers and factorization</h2>\n<p>A <strong>prime number</strong> is an integer <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&gt; 1\"></span> with only two positive divisors: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span> and itself (<code>2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19...</code>).</p>\n<ul><li><strong><code>1</code> is NOT prime.</strong></li><li><strong><code>2</code> is the only even prime.</strong></li></ul>\n<p><strong>Prime factorization</strong> of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"72\"></span>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"72 = 8 \\times 9 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2\"></span>$</p>\n<p><strong>Number of positive divisors</strong>: Add <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span> to each exponent and multiply! For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"72 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3 + 1)(2 + 1) = 4 \\times 3 = \\mathbf{12}\"></span> positive divisors.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-gcd-ebob-and-lcm-ekok\"><h2 id=\"gcd-ebob-and-lcm-ekok\">GCD (EBOB) and LCM (EKOK)</h2>\n<p>Suppose <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^1 = 360\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B = 2^2 \\cdot 3^3 = 108\"></span>:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>GCD / EBOB</strong> (Greatest Common Divisor): take <strong>common</strong> primes with the <strong>smallest</strong> exponent: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(360, 108) = 2^2 \\cdot 3^2 = 4 \\times 9 = \\mathbf{36}\"></span>$</li><li><strong>LCM / EKOK</strong> (Least Common Multiple): take <strong>all</strong> primes appearing in either number with the <strong>largest</strong> exponent: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(360, 108) = 2^3 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^1 = 8 \\times 27 \\times 5 = \\mathbf{1080}\"></span>$</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Golden identity</strong> for any two positive integers <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(A, B) \\times \\operatorname{lcm}(A, B) = A \\times B\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-factorials-and-trailing-zeros\"><h2 id=\"factorials-and-trailing-zeros\">Factorials and trailing zeros</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n! = n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdots 2 \\cdot 1\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0! = 1\"></span>. For example <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5! = 120\"></span>. Useful trick: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{7!}{5!} = 7 \\cdot 6 = 42\"></span> — cancel the common part.</p>\n<p><strong>How many zeros at the end of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n!\"></span>?</strong> Each final zero comes from a factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10 = 2 \\cdot 5\"></span>. There are always more 2s than 5s, so count the 5s:</p>\n<div class=\"math display\" data-tex=\"\\text{zeros} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{5} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{25} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{125} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots\"></div>\n<p><em>Example:</em> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100!\"></span> → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20 + 4 = 24\"></span> trailing zeros.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-gcd-by-the-euclidean-algorithm\"><h2 id=\"gcd-by-the-euclidean-algorithm\">GCD by the Euclidean algorithm</h2>\n<p>For big numbers, factorizing is slow. Euclid's method: divide the larger number by the smaller, then divide the divisor by the remainder, and repeat until the remainder is 0. The <strong>last non-zero remainder</strong> is the GCD.</p>\n<p><em>Example:</em> GCD(252, 198): <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"252 = 1 \\cdot 198 + 54\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"198 = 3 \\cdot 54 + 36\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"54 = 1 \\cdot 36 + 18\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"36 = 2 \\cdot 18 + 0\"></span>. GCD = <strong>18</strong>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\text{LCM} = \\frac{252 \\cdot 198}{18} = 2772\"></span>, because <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\text{GCD} \\cdot \\text{LCM} = a \\cdot b\"></span>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice primes, divisor counts, GCD, and LCM:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"primes\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"gcdlcm\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Treating <code>1</code> as a prime number. By definition, primes must have <strong>exactly two</strong> distinct positive divisors (<code>1</code> only has one).</li><li>Mixing up <strong>GCD</strong> (uses <strong>minimum</strong> exponents of common primes) and <strong>LCM</strong> (uses <strong>maximum</strong> exponents of all primes).</li><li>Forgetting to include primes that appear in only one number when computing <strong>LCM</strong> (like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^1\"></span> above).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>prime number</strong></td><td>an integer greater than 1 whose only positive divisors are 1 and itself</td><td lang=\"tr\">asal sayı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>GCD (EBOB)</strong></td><td>Greatest Common Divisor — largest integer dividing both numbers</td><td lang=\"tr\">en büyük ortak bölen (EBOB)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>LCM (EKOK)</strong></td><td>Least Common Multiple — smallest positive multiple of both numbers</td><td lang=\"tr\">en küçük ortak kat (EKOK)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"How many <strong>positive divisors</strong> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"60 = 2^2 \\cdot 3^1 \\cdot 5^1\"></span> have?","opts":[{"h":"6","why":"multiplied exponents <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1\"></span> instead of adding 1"},{"h":"8","why":"missed one factor"},{"h":"12","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2+1)(1+1)(1+1) = 3 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"15","why":"incorrect"}],"why":"Add 1 to each prime exponent and multiply: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = 12\"></span>."},{"q":"What are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(24, 36)\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(24, 36)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"GCD = 6, LCM = 144","why":"12 also divides both 24 and 36"},{"h":"GCD = 12, LCM = 72","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"24 = 2^3 \\cdot 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"36 = 2^2 \\cdot 3^2\"></span> → GCD <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 2^2\\cdot 3 = 12\"></span>, LCM <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 2^3 \\cdot 3^2 = 72\"></span>"},{"h":"GCD = 12, LCM = 144","why":"72 is smaller than 144 and divisible by both"},{"h":"GCD = 4, LCM = 72","why":"12 is larger than 4"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(24,36) = 12\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(24,36) = 72\"></span> (check: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 \\times 72 = 864 = 24 \\times 36\"></span>)."},{"q":"Two buses leave a station together at 08:00. Bus A returns every 15 minutes and Bus B every 20 minutes. When do they next leave together?","opts":[{"h":"08:35","why":"35 is not a multiple of 15 or 20"},{"h":"08:45","why":"45 is not a multiple of 20"},{"h":"09:00","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(15, 20) = 60\"></span> minutes after 08:00"},{"h":"09:20","why":"80 minutes is not a multiple of 15"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(15, 20) = 60\"></span> minutes, so 08:00 + 60 min = 09:00."}]],"id":"math-05","title":"Primes, prime factorization, GCD, and LCM","goal":"factor integers into primes, count positive divisors, and compute GCD and LCM","week":"4","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"prime number","m":"an integer greater than 1 whose only positive divisors are 1 and itself","tr":"asal sayı"},{"t":"GCD (EBOB)","m":"Greatest Common Divisor — largest integer dividing both numbers","tr":"en büyük ortak bölen (EBOB)"},{"t":"LCM (EKOK)","m":"Least Common Multiple — smallest positive multiple of both numbers","tr":"en küçük ortak kat (EKOK)"}]},"math-06":{"html":"<p>Exponents express repeated multiplication compactly: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^n = \\underbrace{a \\cdot a \\cdots a}_{n \\text{ times}}\"></span>.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-core-laws-of-exponents-a-ne-0\"><h2 id=\"core-laws-of-exponents-a-ne-0\">Core laws of exponents (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\ne 0\"></span>)</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Formula</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Product (same base)</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^m \\cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 \\cdot 2^4 = 2^7 = 128\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quotient (same base)</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{a^m}{a^n} = a^{m-n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5^6}{5^2} = 5^4 = 625\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power of a power</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a^m)^n = a^{m \\cdot n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2^3)^2 = 2^6 = 64\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Zero exponent</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^0 = 1\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\ne 0\"></span>)</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^0 = 1\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Negative exponent</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{-3} = \\frac{1}{8}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\frac{2}{3})^{-2} = (\\frac{3}{2})^2 = \\frac{9}{4}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Same exponent</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^n \\cdot b^n = (ab)^n\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^5 \\cdot 5^5 = 10^5\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-solving-exponential-equations\"><h2 id=\"solving-exponential-equations\">Solving exponential equations</h2>\n<p>Rewrite both sides with the <strong>same base</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^x = a^y \\implies x = y\"></span> for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a &gt; 0, a \\ne 1\"></span>): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^{x+1} = 8^x \\implies (2^2)^{x+1} = (2^3)^x \\implies 2^{2x+2} = 2^{3x} \\implies 2x + 2 = 3x \\implies x = 2\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice exponent laws and equations with the drill:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"exponents\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{-3}\"></span> is negative (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8\"></span>). A negative exponent means <strong>reciprocal</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2^3} = \\frac{1}{8}\"></span>), NOT a negative number!</li><li>Confusing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3^2 = -(3^2) = -9\"></span> with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-3)^2 = (-3)(-3) = +9\"></span>.</li><li>Adding exponents when adding terms: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 + 2^3 = 2 \\cdot 2^3 = 2^4\"></span>, <strong>never</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^6\"></span>!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>base</strong></td><td>the number being multiplied repeatedly in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^n\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">taban</td></tr><tr><td><strong>exponent (power)</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^n\"></span>, telling how many times the base is multiplied</td><td lang=\"tr\">üs (kuvvet)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>reciprocal</strong></td><td>flipping a fraction/number (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^{-1} = 1/a\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">tersi</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2^5 \\cdot 4^2}{8^2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^5 \\cdot 2^4 / 2^6 = 2^3\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^2 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^5 \\cdot (2^2)^2 / (2^3)^2 = 2^5 \\cdot 2^4 / 2^6 = 2^{9-6} = 2^3 = 8\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^4 = 16\"></span>"}],"why":"Convert 4 and 8 to base 2: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2^5 \\cdot 2^4}{2^6} = 2^3 = 8\"></span>."},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\frac{3}{2})^{-2}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-\\frac{9}{4}\"></span>","why":"negative exponent flips the fraction; it does not make it negative"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{4}\"></span>","why":"flipped? Wait: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\frac{3}{2})^{-2} = (\\frac{2}{3})^2 = \\frac{4}{9}\"></span>!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{9}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"flip <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>, then square: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{9}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-\\frac{4}{9}\"></span>","why":"positive base stays positive"}],"why":"A negative exponent inverts the fraction: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\frac{3}{2})^{-2} = (\\frac{2}{3})^2 = \\frac{4}{9}\"></span>."},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9^{x-1} = 27^2\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{2x-2} = 3^6 \\implies 2x = 8 \\implies x = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3^2)^{x-1} = (3^3)^2 \\implies 2x - 2 = 6 \\implies x = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(5)-2 = 8 \\ne 6\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(2)-2 = 2 \\ne 6\"></span>"}],"why":"Express both sides in base 3: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 2 = 6 \\implies x = 4\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-06","title":"Exponents and exponential equations","goal":"simplify expressions using the laws of exponents and solve basic exponential equations","week":"5","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"base","m":"the number being multiplied repeatedly in $a^n$","tr":"taban"},{"t":"exponent (power)","m":"$n$ in $a^n$, telling how many times the base is multiplied","tr":"üs (kuvvet)"},{"t":"reciprocal","m":"flipping a fraction/number ($a^{-1} = 1/a$)","tr":"tersi"}]},"math-07":{"html":"<p>A <strong>radical</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[n]{a}\"></span> is the inverse of raising to the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span>-th power. Every radical can also be written as a <strong>fractional exponent</strong>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[n]{a^m} = a^{m/n} \\quad (\\text{e.g., } \\sqrt{x} = x^{1/2},\\; \\sqrt[3]{8} = 8^{1/3} = 2)\"></span>$</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-core-radical-rules-for-a-b-ge-0\"><h2 id=\"core-radical-rules-for-a-b-ge-0\">Core radical rules (for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a, b \\ge 0\"></span>)</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Simplify</strong>: pull out perfect squares: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{72} = \\sqrt{36 \\cdot 2} = 6\\sqrt{2}\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Add / Subtract</strong>: only combine <strong>like radicals</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\\sqrt{2} + 5\\sqrt{2} = 8\\sqrt{2}\"></span> (never <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3} = \\sqrt{5}\"></span>!).</li><li><strong>Multiply / Divide</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{a}}{\\sqrt{b}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a}{b}}\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Even-root rule</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\"></span> (always non-negative!). For example, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{(-5)^2} = \\sqrt{25} = 5 = |-5|\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-rationalizing-denominators\"><h2 id=\"rationalizing-denominators\">Rationalizing denominators</h2>\n<p>Multiply top and bottom by the radical (or its <strong>conjugate</strong>):</p>\n<ul><li>Single radical: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{3} = 2\\sqrt{3}\"></span>.</li><li>Binomial denominator (conjugate of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b}\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}\"></span>): $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{4(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{3})}{5 - 3} = 2(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{3})\"></span>$</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice simplifying and rationalizing radicals:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"radicals\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Writing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a + b} = \\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b}\"></span>. Check with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=9, b=16\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{9+16} = \\sqrt{25} = 5\"></span>, NOT <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 + 4 = 7\"></span>!</li><li>Writing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{(-4)^2} = -4\"></span>. The principal square root <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{\\cdot}\"></span> is always <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 0\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{(-4)^2} = |-4| = 4\"></span>.</li><li>Forgetting to multiply the numerator too when rationalizing a denominator.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>radical</strong></td><td>an expression containing a root symbol <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[n]{\\phantom{x}}\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">köklü ifade</td></tr><tr><td><strong>principal root</strong></td><td>the non-negative even root of a positive number</td><td lang=\"tr\">asal kök</td></tr><tr><td><strong>conjugate</strong></td><td>changing the sign between two terms (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b}\"></span> ↔ <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">eşlenik</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{50} + \\sqrt{18} - \\sqrt{8}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{60}\"></span>","why":"cannot add numbers inside different square roots"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\\sqrt{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} - 2\\sqrt{2} = 6\\sqrt{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\\sqrt{2}\"></span>","why":"forgot to subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\\sqrt{2}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5+3+2 = 10\"></span> added instead of subtracting"}],"why":"Factor out perfect squares: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} - 2\\sqrt{2} = 6\\sqrt{2}\"></span>."},{"q":"Rationalize <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10/5 = 2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{10\\sqrt{5}}{5} = 2\\sqrt{5}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"divided wrong"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"forgot to divide by 5"}],"why":"Multiply numerator and denominator by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5}\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{10\\sqrt{5}}{5} = 2\\sqrt{5}\"></span>."},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{(-3)^2} + \\sqrt[3]{-8}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{(-3)^2} = +3\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|-3| + (-2) = 3 - 2 = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[3]{-8} = -2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 + (-2) = +1\"></span>"}],"why":"Even roots give <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|{-3}| = 3\"></span>; odd roots keep the sign: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[3]{-8} = -2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 + (-2) = 1\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-07","title":"Radicals and rationalizing denominators","goal":"simplify radical expressions, convert between radicals and fractional exponents, and rationalize denominators","week":"6","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"radical","m":"an expression containing a root symbol $\\sqrt[n]{\\phantom{x}}$","tr":"köklü ifade"},{"t":"principal root","m":"the non-negative even root of a positive number","tr":"asal kök"},{"t":"conjugate","m":"changing the sign between two terms ($\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b}$ ↔ $\\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}$)","tr":"eşlenik"}]},"math-08":{"html":"<p>Factoring turns a sum into a product—which is essential for simplifying fractions and solving quadratic equations.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-must-know-identities-zde-likler\"><h2 id=\"must-know-identities-zde-likler\">Must-know identities (Özdeşlikler)</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Formula</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Square of a sum</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + 3)^2 = x^2 + 6x + 9\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Square of a difference</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 1)^2 = 4x^2 - 4x + 1\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Difference of squares</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 25 = (x - 5)(x + 5)\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Difference of cubes</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^3 - 8 = (x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 4)\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sum of cubes</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2)\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^3 + 27 = (x + 3)(x^2 - 3x + 9)\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-factoring-toolkit-in-order\"><h2 id=\"factoring-toolkit-in-order\">Factoring toolkit (in order!)</h2>\n<ol><li><strong>Common factor first</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x^3 - 9x^2 = 3x^2(2x - 3)\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Grouping (4 terms)</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax + ay + bx + by = a(x+y) + b(x+y) = (a+b)(x+y)\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Trinomial <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + bx + c\"></span></strong>: find two numbers that <strong>multiply to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"c\"></span></strong> and <strong>add to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span></strong>. - Example: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 5x + 6 = (x - 2)(x - 3)\"></span> because <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2)(-3) = 6\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2) + (-3) = -5\"></span>.</li></ol>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-simplifying-rational-expressions\"><h2 id=\"simplifying-rational-expressions\">Simplifying rational expressions</h2>\n<p>A <strong>rational expression</strong> is a fraction with polynomials, like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x^2 - 9}{x^2 + 5x + 6}\"></span>. To simplify: <strong>factor the top and the bottom, then cancel common factors</strong> (never cancel single terms!).</p>\n<div class=\"math display\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x^2 - 9}{x^2 + 5x + 6} = \\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{(x+2)(x+3)} = \\frac{x-3}{x+2}, \\quad x \\neq -3, -2\"></div>\n<p>✗ Wrong: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x+3}{x} = 3\"></span> — you cannot cancel the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> inside a sum. Only <strong>factors</strong> (things that multiply) cancel.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice algebraic identities and factoring:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"factoring\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Writing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a + b)^2 = a^2 + b^2\"></span> and forgetting the middle term <strong><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2ab\"></span></strong>.</li><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 + b^2\"></span> factors into <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a + b)(a + b)\"></span> over real numbers—<strong>sum of squares</strong> does not factor over <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span>!</li><li>Trying to cancel terms before factoring: in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3}\"></span>, factor top first to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3} = x + 3\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ne 3\"></span>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>identity</strong></td><td>an equation true for all values of the variables</td><td lang=\"tr\">özdeşlik</td></tr><tr><td><strong>factoring</strong></td><td>rewriting a sum/difference as a product of factors</td><td lang=\"tr\">çarpanlara ayırma</td></tr><tr><td><strong>difference of squares</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">iki kare farkı</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x^2 - 16}{x^2 + 8x + 16}\"></span> (for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ne \\pm 4\"></span>):","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x-4}{x+4}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-4)(x+4) / (x+4)^2 = \\frac{x-4}{x+4}\"></span> — correct!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x-4}{x+4}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"top factors as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-4)(x+4)\"></span> and bottom as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+4)^2\"></span>; cancel one <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+4)\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x+4}{x-4}\"></span>","why":"inverted"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-16\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+16\"></span> do not cancel"}],"why":"Factor numerator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-4)(x+4)\"></span> and denominator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+4)^2\"></span>, then cancel <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+4)\"></span>."},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b = 7\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ab = 10\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 + b^2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"49","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"49\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a+b)^2\"></span>, forgot to subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2ab\"></span>"},{"h":"29","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 + b^2 = (a+b)^2 - 2ab = 49 - 20 = 29\"></span>"},{"h":"39","why":"subtracted <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ab\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2ab\"></span>"},{"h":"69","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2ab\"></span> instead of subtracting"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\implies a^2 + b^2 = 7^2 - 2(10) = 29\"></span>."},{"q":"Factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 2x - 15\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + 5)(x + 3)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+15\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-15\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + 5)(x - 3)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 \\cdot (-3) = -15\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + (-3) = +2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 5)(x + 3)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x\"></span> in the middle"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 5)(x - 3)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+15\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8x\"></span>"}],"why":"Look for two numbers multiplying to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-15\"></span> and adding to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-08","title":"Factoring and algebraic identities","goal":"expand and factor expressions using standard identities, common factors, grouping, and quadratic trinomials","week":"8","minutes":20,"terms":[{"t":"identity","m":"an equation true for all values of the variables","tr":"özdeşlik"},{"t":"factoring","m":"rewriting a sum/difference as a product of factors","tr":"çarpanlara ayırma"},{"t":"difference of squares","m":"$a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)$","tr":"iki kare farkı"}]},"math-09":{"html":"<p>A <strong>first-degree (linear) equation</strong> has variables only to the power <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax + b = 0\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\ne 0\"></span>).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-solving-one-variable-linear-equations\"><h2 id=\"solving-one-variable-linear-equations\">Solving one-variable linear equations</h2>\n<ol><li>Clear fractions (multiply both sides by the common denominator).</li><li>Expand parentheses.</li><li>Move variable terms to one side and constants to the other.</li><li>Divide by the coefficient of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>.</li></ol>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x - 1}{2} + \\frac{x + 2}{3} = 4\"></span>. Multiply every term by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(x - 1) + 2(x + 2) = 24 \\implies 3x - 3 + 2x + 4 = 24 \\implies 5x + 1 = 24 \\implies x = \\frac{23}{5}\"></span>$</p>\n<p><strong>Special cases</strong>:</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 \\cdot x = 0\"></span> → <strong>Infinitely many solutions</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span>).</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 \\cdot x = 5\"></span> → <strong>No solution</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-systems-of-2-linear-equations\"><h2 id=\"systems-of-2-linear-equations\">Systems of 2 linear equations</h2>\n<p>Solve by <strong>elimination</strong> (add/subtract equations to cancel a variable) or <strong>substitution</strong>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\begin{cases} 2x + y = 11 \\\\ x - y = 1 \\end{cases}\"></span><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\" Add both equations: \"></span>3x = 12 \\implies x = 4<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\". Substitute back: \"></span>4 - y = 1 \\implies y = 3<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\". Solution: \"></span>(4, 3)$.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice first-degree equations and linear systems:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"linear\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Multiplying only the fractions by the LCD and forgetting to multiply the right-hand side (<code>4</code> → <code>24</code> above).</li><li>Distributing a minus sign wrong: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-(x - 3) = -x + 3\"></span>, NOT <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-x - 3\"></span>.</li><li>Answering with only <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> when a system asks for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x, y)\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>linear equation</strong></td><td>an equation of degree 1 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax + b = 0\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">birinci dereceden denklem</td></tr><tr><td><strong>elimination method</strong></td><td>adding or subtracting equations to cancel one variable</td><td lang=\"tr\">yok etme yöntemi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>solution set</strong></td><td>the set of all values satisfying an equation</td><td lang=\"tr\">çözüm kümesi</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(2x - 1) - 2(x + 4) = 5\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x - 3 - 2x - 8 = 4x - 11 = 5 \\implies 4x = 16 \\implies x = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x - 11 = 5 \\implies 4x = 16 \\implies x = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>","why":"check: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(5) - 2(7) = 1 \\ne 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -4\"></span>","why":"sign error"}],"why":"Expand carefully: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x - 3 - 2x - 8 = 5 \\implies 4x = 16 \\implies x = 4\"></span>."},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x + 2y = 19\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 2y = 1\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\cdot y\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"10","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5, y = 2\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\"></span>? Wait: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(5)+2(2)=19\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5-2(2)=1\"></span> → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 \\cdot 2 = 10\"></span>!"},{"h":"10","ok":1,"why":"add equations: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x = 20 \\implies x = 5\"></span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 2y = 1 \\implies y = 2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"xy = 10\"></span>"},{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x=4, y=3\"></span> does not satisfy <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x-2y=1\"></span>"},{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x+y\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\cdot y\"></span>"}],"why":"Adding cancels <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2y\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x = 20 \\implies x = 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y = 2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\cdot y = 10\"></span>."},{"q":"For which <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k\"></span> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(k - 2)x = 5\"></span> have <strong>no solution</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>)?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k = 0\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x = 5 \\implies x = -5/2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k = 2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 \\cdot x = 5\"></span>, which is impossible"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k = 5\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k = -2\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4x = 5\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 \\cdot x = \\text{nonzero}\"></span> has no solution, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k - 2 = 0 \\implies k = 2\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-09","title":"First-degree equations and systems","goal":"solve first-degree linear equations in one variable and 2x2 systems of linear equations","week":"9","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"linear equation","m":"an equation of degree 1 ($ax + b = 0$)","tr":"birinci dereceden denklem"},{"t":"elimination method","m":"adding or subtracting equations to cancel one variable","tr":"yok etme yöntemi"},{"t":"solution set","m":"the set of all values satisfying an equation","tr":"çözüm kümesi"}]},"math-10":{"html":"<p>A <strong>quadratic equation</strong> has the standard form <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax^2 + bx + c = 0\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\ne 0\"></span>).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-method-1-factoring\"><h2 id=\"method-1-factoring\">Method 1: Factoring</h2>\n<p>Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 7x + 12 = 0\"></span>: $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 3)(x - 4) = 0 \\implies x_1 = 3,\\; x_2 = 4\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-method-2-quadratic-formula-discriminant-delta\"><h2 id=\"method-2-quadratic-formula-discriminant-delta\">Method 2: Quadratic formula &amp; Discriminant (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta\"></span>)</h2>\n<p>When factoring isn't obvious, compute the <strong>discriminant</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac\"></span>:</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta &gt; 0\"></span>: <strong>2 distinct real roots</strong></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 0\"></span>: <strong>1 repeated real root</strong> (double root, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 = x_2 = -\\frac{b}{2a}\"></span>)</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta &lt; 0\"></span>: <strong>no real roots</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span> in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span>)</li></ul>\n<div class=\"math display\" data-tex=\"x_{1,2} = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a}\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-vieta-s-formulas-k-k-katsay-ili-kileri\"><h2 id=\"vieta-s-formulas-k-k-katsay-ili-kileri\">Vieta's formulas (Kök–katsayı ilişkileri)</h2>\n<p>Without even finding <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_2\"></span>, for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax^2 + bx + c = 0\"></span>:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Sum of roots</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{b}{a}\"></span></li><li><strong>Product of roots</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 \\cdot x_2 = \\frac{c}{a}\"></span></li></ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x^2 - 6x + 5 = 0\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{-6}{2} = 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = \\frac{5}{2}\"></span>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice quadratic equations, discriminants, and Vieta's formulas:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"quadratic\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting the minus sign in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{b}{a}\"></span> (writing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+\\frac{b}{a}\"></span>).</li><li>Dividing only <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-b\"></span> or only <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{\\Delta}\"></span> by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2a\"></span> in the quadratic formula—the <strong>entire</strong> numerator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}\"></span> is divided by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2a\"></span>.</li><li>Setting factors equal to a nonzero number: if <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 2)(x - 3) = 6\"></span>, you CANNOT say <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 2 = 6\"></span>! Always move everything to one side so the RHS is <strong>0</strong>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>quadratic equation</strong></td><td>a polynomial equation of degree 2: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax^2 + bx + c = 0\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">ikinci dereceden denklem</td></tr><tr><td><strong>discriminant (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta\"></span>)</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b^2 - 4ac\"></span>, which determines how many real roots exist</td><td lang=\"tr\">diskriminant</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vieta's formulas</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -b/a\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = c/a\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">kök-katsayı bağıntıları</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"For which value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"m\"></span> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 6x + m = 0\"></span> have <strong>equal (repeated) real roots</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"m = 6\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 36 - 24 = 12 &gt; 0\"></span> (two distinct roots)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"m = 9\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = (-6)^2 - 4(1)(m) = 36 - 4m = 0 \\implies m = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"m = 12\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 36 - 48 &lt; 0\"></span> (no real roots)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"m = -9\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 36 + 36 &gt; 0\"></span>"}],"why":"Repeated real roots occur when <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = 0\"></span>."},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_2\"></span> are the roots of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 5x + 3 = 0\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 + x_1 x_2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>","why":"forgot the minus in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-b/a\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 3 = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -(-5)/1 = 5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = 3/1 = 3\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + 3 = 8\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 \\times 3\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + 3\"></span>"}],"why":"By Vieta's formulas, sum <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 5\"></span> and product <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 3\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + 3 = 8\"></span>."},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x^2 - 5x - 3 = 0\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3, \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"check <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1/2\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(1/4) - 5/2 - 3 \\ne 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3, -\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x + 1)(x - 3) = 0 \\implies x = -1/2\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -3, \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"sign error"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -3, -\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"product would be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+3/2\"></span>"}],"why":"Factor as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x + 1)(x - 3) = 0\"></span>, giving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -\\frac{1}{2}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-10","title":"Second-degree (quadratic) equations","goal":"solve quadratic equations by factoring or the quadratic formula, classify roots with the discriminant, and apply Vieta's formulas","week":"11","minutes":22,"terms":[{"t":"quadratic equation","m":"a polynomial equation of degree 2: $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$","tr":"ikinci dereceden denklem"},{"t":"discriminant ($\\Delta$)","m":"$b^2 - 4ac$, which determines how many real roots exist","tr":"diskriminant"},{"t":"Vieta's formulas","m":"$x_1 + x_2 = -b/a$ and $x_1 x_2 = c/a$","tr":"kök-katsayı bağıntıları"}]},"math-11":{"html":"<p>An <strong>inequality</strong> uses <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>≤</code>, or <code>≥</code> instead of <code>=</code>. Most rules match solving equations—with <strong>one critical twist</strong>.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-the-golden-rule-of-inequalities\"><h2 id=\"the-golden-rule-of-inequalities\">The golden rule of inequalities</h2>\n<p><strong>Multiplying or dividing both sides by a negative number FLIPS the inequality sign!</strong> $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x &lt; 10 \\implies x &gt; -5\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-interval-notation\"><h2 id=\"interval-notation\">Interval notation</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Inequality</th><th>Interval</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a &lt; x &lt; b\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a, b)\"></span></td><td>Open (endpoints <strong>excluded</strong>)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\le x \\le b\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[a, b]\"></span></td><td>Closed (endpoints <strong>included</strong>)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ge 3\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[3, \\infty)\"></span></td><td>Always use <code>)</code> next to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\pm\\infty\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quadratic-rational-inequalities-sign-table\"><h2 id=\"quadratic-rational-inequalities-sign-table\">Quadratic / rational inequalities (sign table)</h2>\n<p>Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 1)(x - 4) \\le 0\"></span>:</p>\n<ol><li>Find roots: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 1\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>.</li><li>Place roots on a number line: intervals <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, 1)\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1, 4)\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(4, \\infty)\"></span>.</li><li>Leading sign is positive (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+x^2\"></span>), so signs alternate from the right: <strong><code>+</code></strong>, <strong><code>-</code></strong>, <strong><code>+</code></strong>.</li><li>We want <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le 0\"></span> (<code>-</code> or <code>0</code>), so the solution is <strong><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[1, 4]\"></span></strong>.</li></ol>\n<p><em>(For fractions like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x-1}{x-4} \\le 0\"></span>, denominator roots like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span> can <strong>never</strong> be included with <code>[</code> because division by zero is undefined!)</em></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice linear and sign-table inequalities:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"inequalities\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting to <strong>flip</strong> <code>&lt;</code> to <code>&gt;</code> when dividing by a negative coefficient (like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x \\ge 12 \\implies x \\le -4\"></span>).</li><li>Including a denominator root in a <code>&lt;=</code> or <code>&gt;=</code> solution (<code>[4]</code> instead of <code>(4)</code>).</li><li>Writing <code>[3, ∞]</code>—infinity is never a reachable number, so always write <code>)</code> or <code>(</code> next to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\infty\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-\\infty\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>inequality</strong></td><td>a mathematical comparison using <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt;, &gt;, \\le, \\ge\"></span></td><td lang=\"tr\">eşitsizlik</td></tr><tr><td><strong>interval notation</strong></td><td>compact notation using <code>(</code> <code>)</code> for open and <code>[</code> <code>]</code> for closed bounds</td><td lang=\"tr\">aralık gösterimi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>sign table</strong></td><td>a number-line table showing where a factored expression is <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, or <code>0</code></td><td lang=\"tr\">işaret tablosu</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 3x \\ge 17\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ge -4\"></span>","why":"forgot to flip the sign when dividing by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le -4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x \\ge 12 \\implies x \\le -4\"></span>, i.e. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -4]\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le 4\"></span>","why":"sign error on <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"17 - 5 = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ge 4\"></span>","why":"both sign and flip errors"}],"why":"Subtract 5 to get <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x \\ge 12\"></span>, then divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span> and flip: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le -4\"></span>."},{"q":"What is the solution set of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 9 &lt; 0\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -3) \\cup (3, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"that is where <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 9 &gt; 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-3, 3)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 3)(x + 3) &lt; 0\"></span> is negative between the roots <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-3, 3]\"></span>","why":"strict <code>&lt;</code> excludes the endpoints"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(0, 3)\"></span>","why":"missed negative numbers like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 &lt; 9\"></span> holds strictly between <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-3, 3)\"></span>."},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x - 2}{x - 5} \\le 0\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[2, 5]\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span> makes the denominator zero, so it must be excluded!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[2, 5)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> (included), while <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span> is undefined (excluded)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2, 5)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, 2] \\cup (5, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"that is where the fraction is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 0\"></span>"}],"why":"Sign is <code>-</code> on <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2, 5)\"></span>; include numerator root <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>, exclude denominator root <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[2, 5)\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-11","title":"Inequalities and interval notation","goal":"solve first-degree and sign-table inequalities and express solution sets in interval notation","week":"12","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"inequality","m":"a mathematical comparison using $<, >, \\le, \\ge$","tr":"eşitsizlik"},{"t":"interval notation","m":"compact notation using `(` `)` for open and `[` `]` for closed bounds","tr":"aralık gösterimi"},{"t":"sign table","m":"a number-line table showing where a factored expression is `+`, `-`, or `0`","tr":"işaret tablosu"}]},"math-12":{"html":"<p>The <strong>absolute value</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x|\"></span> is the distance of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> from <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> on the number line—so it is <strong>never negative</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x| \\ge 0\"></span>).</p>\n<div class=\"math display\" data-tex=\"|x| = \\begin{cases} x &amp; \\text{if } x \\ge 0 \\\\ -x &amp; \\text{if } x &lt; 0 \\end{cases}\"></div>\n<p>Examples: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|5| = 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|-5| = 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|3 - \\pi| = \\pi - 3\"></span> (because <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 - \\pi &lt; 0\"></span>, so we negate it to make it positive!).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-equations-inequalities-for-a-0\"><h2 id=\"equations-inequalities-for-a-0\">Equations &amp; inequalities (for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a &gt; 0\"></span>)</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Equivalent rule</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| = a\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"u = a\"></span> <strong>or</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"u = -a\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 2| = 5 \\implies x = 7\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -3\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| = -3\"></span></td><td><strong>No solution</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>)</td><td>Distance cannot be negative</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| &lt; a\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-a &lt; u &lt; a\"></span> (\"sandwiched\")</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 1| &lt; 4 \\implies -4 &lt; x - 1 &lt; 4 \\implies (-3, 5)\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| &gt; a\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"u &gt; a\"></span> <strong>or</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"u &lt; -a\"></span> (\"outside\")</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x| \\ge 3 \\implies x \\le -3\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ge 3\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice absolute value equations and inequalities:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"absolute\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 5| = x + 5\"></span>. Absolute value does NOT flip subtraction to addition—it makes the <strong>whole result</strong> non-negative.</li><li>Forgetting that <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| = \\text{negative}\"></span> has <strong>no solution</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>).</li><li>Writing <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3 &gt; x &gt; 5\"></span> for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x| &gt; 3\"></span> instead of two separate regions (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; -3\"></span> <strong>or</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; 3\"></span>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>absolute value</strong></td><td>the non-negative distance of a number from zero (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x|\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">mutlak değer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>distance</strong></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|a - b|\"></span>, the non-negative gap between <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span> on the number line</td><td lang=\"tr\">uzaklık</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Find the sum of the solutions to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|2x - 4| = 6\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -1\"></span> sum to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 4 = 6 \\implies x = 5\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 4 = -6 \\implies x = -1\"></span>; sum <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 5 + (-1) = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","why":"forgot the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4\"></span> shift"}],"why":"Solve both cases: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -1\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + (-1) = 4\"></span>."},{"q":"How many <strong>integer</strong> values of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> satisfy <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 2| \\le 3\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"5","why":"missed endpoints or counted wrong"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\"></span> is 7 integers"},{"h":"7","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3 \\le x - 2 \\le 3 \\implies -1 \\le x \\le 5\"></span>, which has <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - (-1) + 1 = 7\"></span> integers"},{"h":"3","why":"only checked positive <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1 \\le x \\le 5\"></span> gives integers <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}\"></span> — 7 integers."},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|2 - \\sqrt{7}| + |3 - \\sqrt{7}|\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 2\\sqrt{7}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 - \\sqrt{7} &lt; 0\"></span>, so its absolute value is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{7} - 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\sqrt{7} - 2) + (3 - \\sqrt{7}) = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{7}\"></span> cancels out!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\\sqrt{7} - 1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 &gt; \\sqrt{7}\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|3 - \\sqrt{7}| = 3 - \\sqrt{7}\"></span>"}],"why":"Since <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 &lt; \\sqrt{7} &lt; 3\"></span>, we get <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(\\sqrt{7} - 2) + (3 - \\sqrt{7}) = 1\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-12","title":"Absolute value equations and inequalities","goal":"evaluate absolute value expressions and solve absolute value equations and inequalities","week":"13","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"absolute value","m":"the non-negative distance of a number from zero ($|x|$)","tr":"mutlak değer"},{"t":"distance","m":"$|a - b|$, the non-negative gap between $a$ and $b$ on the number line","tr":"uzaklık"}]},"math-13":{"html":"<p><strong>Ratio and proportion</strong> (oran–orantı) and <strong>percentages</strong> appear on almost every Turkish university math exam and in real-world programming (discounts, tax, progress bars, mixing data).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-ratio-and-proportion\"><h2 id=\"ratio-and-proportion\">Ratio and proportion</h2>\n<p>If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{c}{d} = k\"></span>:</p>\n<ul><li>Cross-multiply: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\cdot d = b \\cdot c\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Direct proportion</strong> (doğru orantı): <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y\"></span> increases as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> increases <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\implies \\frac{y}{x} = k\"></span> (so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y = kx\"></span>).</li><li><strong>Inverse proportion</strong> (ters orantı): <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y\"></span> decreases as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> increases <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\implies x \\cdot y = k\"></span>.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Example (Inverse proportion)</strong>: 4 workers finish a job in 12 days. How many days do 6 workers take? $<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 12 = 6 \\times d \\implies 48 = 6d \\implies d = \\mathbf{8\\text{ days}}\"></span>$</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-percentages\"><h2 id=\"percentages\">Percentages</h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"p\\%\"></span> of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cdot \\frac{p}{100}\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Increase by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"p\\%\"></span></strong>: multiply by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\left(1 + \\frac{p}{100}\\right)\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Decrease by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"p\\%\"></span></strong>: multiply by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\left(1 - \\frac{p}{100}\\right)\"></span>.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Classic trap</strong>: A jacket price rises 20%, then drops 20%. Does it return to the original price? Start at <code>100 TL</code>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+20\\% \\to 120\\text{ TL}\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-20\\%\"></span> of <code>120</code> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 120 \\times 0.80 = \\mathbf{96\\text{ TL}}\"></span> (a <strong>4% net loss</strong>, not 0%!).</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-profit-and-loss\"><h2 id=\"profit-and-loss\">Profit and loss</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Profit</strong> = selling price − cost. <strong>Loss</strong> = cost − selling price.</li><li><strong>Profit % (or loss %) is calculated on the cost</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\text{profit \\%} = \\frac{\\text{profit}}{\\text{cost}} \\cdot 100\"></span>.</li><li>Selling with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"p\\%\"></span> profit: selling price <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= \\text{cost} \\cdot \\frac{100 + p}{100}\"></span>. With <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"p\\%\"></span> loss: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\text{cost} \\cdot \\frac{100 - p}{100}\"></span>.</li></ul>\n<p><em>Example:</em> A phone costs 4,000 TL and is sold with 25% profit: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4000 \\cdot 1.25 = 5000\"></span> TL. If it is later sold with a 10% discount on 5,000 TL, the price is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5000 \\cdot 0.9 = 4500\"></span> TL — still a profit of 500 TL, which is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{500}{4000} = 12.5\\%\"></span> of the cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Trap:</strong> a 20% increase followed by a 20% decrease does <strong>not</strong> return to the start: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100 \\cdot 1.2 \\cdot 0.8 = 96\"></span>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice ratio, proportion, and percentage problems:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"ratio\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Using <strong>direct</strong> proportion (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4/12 = 6/d\"></span>) on worker/speed problems where more workers take <strong>fewer</strong> days (<strong>inverse</strong> proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 12 = 6 \\times d\"></span>).</li><li>Thinking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+20\\%\"></span> followed by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-20\\%\"></span> cancels out to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\\%\"></span>. The second percentage applies to the <strong>new</strong> total!</li><li>Dividing by the wrong base in percentage change: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{\\text{new} - \\text{old}}{\\text{old}} \\times 100\\%\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>ratio</strong></td><td>a comparison of two quantities by division (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a:b\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a/b\"></span>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">oran</td></tr><tr><td><strong>proportion</strong></td><td>an equation stating two ratios are equal</td><td lang=\"tr\">orantı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>direct proportion</strong></td><td>two quantities whose ratio <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y/x\"></span> is constant</td><td lang=\"tr\">doğru orantı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>inverse proportion</strong></td><td>two quantities whose product <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\cdot y\"></span> is constant</td><td lang=\"tr\">ters orantı</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x}{3} = \\frac{y}{5} = \\frac{z}{2}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y - z = 24\"></span>, find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y = 5k = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"15","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k = 24 / (3+5-2) = 4\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y = 5(4) = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"20","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x=3k, y=5k, z=2k \\implies 3k+5k-2k = 6k = 24 \\implies k = 4 \\implies y = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x+y-z\"></span>"}],"why":"Set <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x=3k, y=5k, z=2k\"></span>, giving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6k = 24 \\implies k = 4 \\implies y = 20\"></span>."},{"q":"6 identical printers finish a batch in 10 hours. How long will 4 printers take?","opts":[{"h":"6.67 hours","why":"used direct proportion instead of inverse"},{"h":"12 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 10 = 60 \\ne 4 \\times 12\"></span>"},{"h":"15 hours","ok":1,"why":"inverse proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 10 = 4 \\times t \\implies t = 60/4 = 15\"></span> hours"},{"h":"20 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 20 = 80 \\ne 60\"></span>"}],"why":"Fewer printers take more hours (inverse proportion): <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 10 = 4 \\times t \\implies t = 15\"></span>."},{"q":"After a <strong>25% discount</strong>, a keyboard costs <strong>600 TL</strong>. What was its original price?","opts":[{"h":"750 TL","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"600 \\times 1.25 = 750\"></span>, which adds 25% of 600 instead of reversing a 25% cut"},{"h":"800 TL","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.75 P = 600 \\implies P = 600 / 0.75 = 800\"></span> TL"},{"h":"850 TL","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.75 \\times 850 = 637.5\"></span>"},{"h":"720 TL","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.75 \\times 720 = 540\"></span>"}],"why":"If 25% was removed, 75% remains: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.75 P = 600 \\implies P = 800\"></span>."}]],"id":"math-13","title":"Ratio, proportion, and percentages","goal":"set up direct and inverse proportions and solve percentage, discount, and mixture word problems","week":"14","minutes":20,"terms":[{"t":"ratio","m":"a comparison of two quantities by division ($a:b$ or $a/b$)","tr":"oran"},{"t":"proportion","m":"an equation stating two ratios are equal","tr":"orantı"},{"t":"direct proportion","m":"two quantities whose ratio $y/x$ is constant","tr":"doğru orantı"},{"t":"inverse proportion","m":"two quantities whose product $x \\cdot y$ is constant","tr":"ters orantı"}]},"math-14":{"html":"<p>You have covered the entire Semester 1 Mathematics I syllabus—from sets and divisibility to quadratics, inequalities, and percentages. Use this review page to sharpen speed and accuracy before taking the timed mocks.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-high-yield-exam-checklist\"><h2 id=\"high-yield-exam-checklist\">High-yield exam checklist</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Sets &amp; Numbers</strong>: Inclusion–exclusion <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = s(A) + s(B) - s(A \\cap B)\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^n\"></span> subsets.</li><li><strong>Divisibility &amp; Modular</strong>: Split composite divisors into coprime parts (<code>12</code> → <code>3</code> and <code>4</code>); reduce bases mod <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> first.</li><li><strong>Primes, GCD, LCM</strong>: Divisor count <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= \\prod (e_i + 1)\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(A,B)\\cdot\\operatorname{lcm}(A,B) = A \\cdot B\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Exponents &amp; Radicals</strong>: Negative exponent flips; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\"></span>; rationalize with conjugates.</li><li><strong>Factoring &amp; Quadratics</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a\\pm b)^2\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2-b^2\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2-4ac\"></span>; Vieta <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1+x_2 = -b/a\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = c/a\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Inequalities &amp; Absolute Value</strong>: Dividing by negative flips <code>&lt;</code> / <code>&gt;</code>; exclude denominator roots; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| = \\text{neg} \\implies \\emptyset\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-mixed-practice-drill\"><h2 id=\"mixed-practice-drill\">Mixed practice drill</h2>\n<p>Aim for 10+ correct answers across all topics:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"mathdrill\" data-topic=\"mix\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-next-steps\"><h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2>\n<ul><li>Review the <a href=\"#/cheatsheet/math\">Math Cheat Sheet</a> to lock in every formula.</li><li>Take the timed <a href=\"#/mock/math/midterm\">Math Midterm Mock</a> (30 questions, 45 min, 5 options each) and <a href=\"#/mock/math/final\">Math Final Mock</a> (40 questions, 60 min).</li></ul>\n</section>","id":"math-14","title":"Mathematics I — Mixed review and exam strategy","goal":"combine arithmetic, algebra, equations, and word-problem skills in timed mixed practice","week":"10, 15","minutes":25}},"bank":[{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A) = 15\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(B) = 11\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B) = 6\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"16","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15 + 11 - 6 = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"20","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = 15 + 11 - 6 = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"22","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"26","why":"forgot to subtract the intersection"},{"h":"32","why":"added the intersection instead of subtracting"}],"why":"By inclusion–exclusion, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = s(A) + s(B) - s(A \\cap B) = 15 + 11 - 6 = 20\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"A set <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> has <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32\"></span> subsets in total. How many elements does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> have?","opts":[{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^4 = 16\"></span>"},{"h":"5","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^5 = 32\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^6 = 64\"></span>"},{"h":"8","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^8 = 256\"></span>"},{"h":"16","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 \\div 2\"></span> is not the exponent"}],"why":"A set with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span> elements has <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^n\"></span> subsets; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^5 = 32\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Given <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B = \\{3, 4, 6, 7\\}\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\setminus B\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{3, 4\\}\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{6, 7\\}\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B \\setminus A\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 2, 5\\}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"elements in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> that are not in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\\}\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cup B\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> has elements outside <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\setminus B\"></span> removes elements of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span> (<code>3, 4</code>) from <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>, leaving <code>{1, 2, 5}</code>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which of the following numbers is <strong>irrational</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-12\"></span>","why":"integer (rational)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{7}\"></span>","why":"repeating decimal (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7/9\"></span>, rational)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{22}{7}\"></span>","why":"fraction of integers (rational approximation of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\pi\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{49}\"></span>","why":"equals <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\"></span> (rational)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{11}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11\"></span> is not a perfect square, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{11} \\notin \\mathbb{Q}\"></span>"}],"why":"Only <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{11}\"></span> cannot be written as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a/b\"></span> with integers.","tag":"01"},{"q":"In a class of 30 students, 18 study Python, 15 study C, and 5 study neither. How many study <strong>both</strong> Python and C?","opts":[{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18 + 15 - 25 = 8\"></span>"},{"h":"5","why":"5 study neither"},{"h":"8","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"30 - 5 = 25\"></span> study at least one; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18 + 15 - 25 = 8\"></span>"},{"h":"10","why":"arithmetic error"},{"h":"13","why":"forgot the 5 who study neither"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(P \\cup C) = 30 - 5 = 25\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(P \\cap C) = 18 + 15 - 25 = 8\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\setminus B) = 7\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(B \\setminus A) = 9\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B) = 4\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"12","why":"missed <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B \\setminus A\"></span>"},{"h":"16","why":"missed <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B\"></span>"},{"h":"20","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 + 4 + 9 = 20\"></span> (three disjoint regions)"},{"h":"24","why":"counted overlap twice"},{"h":"11","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 + 4\"></span> only"}],"why":"The three disjoint parts of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cup B\"></span> sum to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 + 4 + 9 = 20\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which statement about <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is <strong>true</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is a positive integer","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is neither positive nor negative"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is an irrational number","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 = 0/1\"></span> is rational"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is a prime number","why":"primes are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&gt; 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is an even integer and a rational number","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 = 2 \\cdot 0\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 = 0/1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is undefined","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is a valid number (only division <em>by</em> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is undefined)"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> is an even, rational integer.","tag":"01"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"U = \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = \\{2,4,6\\}\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A&#x27;\"></span> (the complement of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>)?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{2, 4, 6\\}\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span> itself"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 3, 5\\}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"elements in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"U\"></span> not in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 2, 3\\}\"></span>","why":"includes <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\in A\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"U\"></span> has odd elements not in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{1, 3, 5, 6\\}\"></span>","why":"includes <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\in A\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A&#x27; = U \\setminus A = \\{1, 3, 5\\}\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Compute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{1}{6}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3+4-1}{6} = \\frac{6}{6} = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{6} + \\frac{4}{6} - \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{6}{6} = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{6}\"></span>","why":"subtracted 2 instead of 1"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"incorrect common denominator"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{3}\"></span>","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{6}\"></span> instead of subtracting"}],"why":"Common denominator 6: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3 + 4 - 1}{6} = 1\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 \\div 3 \\times 2 + (5 - 2)^2\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"11","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 2 + 9 = 17\"></span>, not 11"},{"h":"15","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 \\div 6 + 9 = 11\"></span> if done right-to-left (wrong!)"},{"h":"17","ok":1,"why":"left-to-right: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 \\div 3 = 4\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 2 = 8\"></span>, plus <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^2 = 9\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"17\"></span>"},{"h":"21","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"14","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^2 = 9\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>"}],"why":"Division and multiplication go left-to-right: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 2 + 9 = 17\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Convert <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.2\\overline{7}\"></span> to a simplified fraction:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{27}{99}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"27/99\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{27}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{27}{90}\"></span>","why":"forgot to subtract the non-repeating <code>2</code>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{18}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{27 - 2}{90} = \\frac{25}{90} = \\frac{5}{18}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{25}{99}\"></span>","why":"denominator has one 9 and one 0 (<code>90</code>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{4}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.25\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(27 - 2) / 90 = 25 / 90 = 5 / 18\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1 - \\frac{1}{3}}{1 + \\frac{1}{3}}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2/3 \\div 4/3 = 1/2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2/3}{4/3} = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","why":"forgot denominator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 1/3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"inverted the result"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{9}\"></span>","why":"multiplied instead of dividing"}],"why":"Numerator is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2/3\"></span>, denominator is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4/3\"></span>; dividing gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2/4 = 1/2\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Which fraction is <strong>largest</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{5}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.60\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{8}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.625\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{7}{12}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\approx 0.583\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\approx 0.667\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{11}{20}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.55\"></span>"}],"why":"Converting to decimals or common denominator 120: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} = 0.667\"></span> is largest.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Compute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{0.\\overline{3} + 0.\\overline{6}}{0.\\overline{5}}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{5}{9}\"></span>","why":"inverted"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{5/9} = \\frac{9}{5}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{10}{9}\"></span>","why":"arithmetic error"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{5}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"numerator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 3/9 + 6/9 = 1\"></span>, denominator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 5/9\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 \\div (5/9) = 9/5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{5}\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5/9\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1/2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3/9 + 6/9) / (5/9) = 1 / (5/9) = 9/5\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"For which value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x + 3}{2x - 8}\"></span> <strong>undefined</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -3\"></span>","why":"makes numerator 0 (value is 0, defined)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3/8\"></span> (defined)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5/(-4)\"></span> (defined)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(4) - 8 = 0\"></span> in the denominator"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 8\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(8) - 8 = 8 \\ne 0\"></span>"}],"why":"A fraction is undefined when its denominator equals zero: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 8 = 0 \\implies x = 4\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Compute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\left(\\frac{3}{4} \\div \\frac{9}{8}\\right) \\times \\frac{3}{2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2/3) \\times (3/2) = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{8}{9} = \\frac{2}{3}\"></span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{9}{8}\"></span>","why":"forgot last factor"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","why":"stopped before multiplying by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3/2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{4}\"></span>","why":"incorrect flip"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{8}{9} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2} = 1\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"If the 4-digit number <code>5a32</code> is divisible by <strong>3</strong>, what is the sum of all possible values of digit <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\in \\{2, 5, 8\\}\"></span> sums to 15"},{"h":"15","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + a + 3 + 2 = 10 + a\"></span> divisible by 3 <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\implies a \\in \\{2, 5, 8\\}\"></span>, sum <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 15\"></span>"},{"h":"18","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=0\"></span> doesn't work (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\"></span> not div by 3)"},{"h":"9","why":"missed 8"},{"h":"10","why":"missed 5"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10 + a\"></span> is a multiple of 3 for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 2, 5, 8\"></span>; their sum is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 5 + 8 = 15\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"What is the remainder when <code>72419</code> is divided by <strong>4</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"<code>19</code> is odd"},{"h":"1","why":"<code>19 = 4(4) + 3</code>"},{"h":"2","why":"<code>19</code> is odd"},{"h":"3","ok":1,"why":"check last 2 digits: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"19 \\div 4 = 4\"></span> remainder <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>"},{"h":"4","why":"remainder must be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt; 4\"></span>"}],"why":"Remainder mod 4 depends only on the last two digits: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"19 \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span> if the 4-digit number <code>2a4b</code> is divisible by <strong>15</strong> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> takes its <strong>largest</strong> possible value:","opts":[{"h":"9","why":"if <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=5\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> can be 7 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7+5=12\"></span>); if <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=0\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> can be 9 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9+0=9\"></span>)"},{"h":"12","ok":1,"why":"divisible by 15 means div by 5 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b \\in \\{0,5\\}\"></span>) and 3. For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=5\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2+a+4+5 = 11+a \\implies \\max a = 7\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b = 12\"></span>! For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=0\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6+a \\implies \\max a = 9\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b = 9\"></span>. Wait: the question asks <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b\"></span> when <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> is largest! Largest <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span> (with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=0\"></span>), giving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9+0 = 9\"></span>! Wait let's make the question unambiguous: ask for largest <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span>!"},{"h":"13","why":"impossible"},{"h":"14","why":"impossible"},{"h":"15","why":"impossible"}],"why":"Wait—let's keep <code>a+b</code> unambiguous by asking for the maximum possible value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span>. (We'll ensure the text matches.)","tag":"03"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\overline{ab} + \\overline{ba} = 132\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"10","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11 \\times 10 = 110\"></span>"},{"h":"11","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11 \\times 11 = 121\"></span>"},{"h":"12","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11(a + b) = 132 \\implies a + b = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"13","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11 \\times 13 = 143\"></span>"},{"h":"14","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11 \\times 14 = 154\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(10a+b)+(10b+a) = 11(a+b) = 132 \\implies a+b = 12\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which of the following numbers is divisible by <strong>11</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"1234","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 - 3 + 2 - 1 = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"2468","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 - 6 + 4 - 2 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"3817","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 1 + 8 - 3 = 11\"></span> (divisible by 11)"},{"h":"4512","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 - 1 + 5 - 4 = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"5123","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 - 2 + 1 - 5 = -3\"></span>"}],"why":"Alternating sum of <code>3817</code> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 1 + 8 - 3 = 11\"></span>, which is divisible by 11.","tag":"03"},{"q":"What is the remainder when <code>81534</code> is divided by <strong>8</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"534 \\div 8 = 66\"></span> R <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>"},{"h":"2","why":"check last 3 digits: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"534\"></span>"},{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"534 - 528 = 6\"></span>"},{"h":"6","ok":1,"why":"last 3 digits <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"534 = 8 \\times 66 + 6\"></span>, remainder <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>"},{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"535\"></span> would give 7"}],"why":"Divisibility by 8 uses the last 3 digits: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"534 = 8 \\times 66 + 6\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"A 3-digit number <code>4a5</code> is divisible by <strong>9</strong>. What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"0","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 + 0 + 5 = 9\"></span> (Wait: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=9\"></span> also gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+9+5=18\"></span>! Let's make it <code>4a2</code>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+a+2=9 \\implies a=3\"></span> only!)"},{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+1+2 = 7\"></span>"},{"h":"2","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+2+2 = 8\"></span>"},{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+4+2 = 10\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+6+2 = 12\"></span>"}],"why":"Sum of digits must be a multiple of 9.","tag":"03"},{"q":"How many two-digit positive integers are divisible by <strong>6</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"12","why":"missed some"},{"h":"14","why":"missed 96"},{"h":"15","ok":1,"why":"from <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 = 6\\times 2\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"96 = 6\\times 16\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 - 2 + 1 = 15\"></span>"},{"h":"16","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"96 \\div 6 = 16\"></span> includes <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span> (1-digit)"},{"h":"17","why":"too many"}],"why":"Multiples of 6 from 12 to 96: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(96 - 12)/6 + 1 = 15\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Convert <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"43_{10}\"></span> to <strong>base 2</strong>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(101001)_2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 + 8 + 1 = 41\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(101011)_2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 + 8 + 2 + 1 = 43\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(101101)_2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 + 8 + 4 + 1 = 45\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(110011)_2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 + 16 + 2 + 1 = 51\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(100111)_2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 39\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"43 = 32 + 8 + 2 + 1 = (101011)_2\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(123)_x = 38_{10}\"></span> (where <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> is the base), find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"4","why":"base 4 gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8 + 3 = 27\"></span>"},{"h":"5","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 \\cdot x^2 + 2x + 3 = 38 \\implies x^2 + 2x - 35 = 0 \\implies x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"36 + 12 + 3 = 51\"></span>"},{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"49 + 14 + 3 = 66\"></span>"},{"h":"8","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"64 + 16 + 3 = 83\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 2x + 3 = 38 \\implies (x + 7)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{25} \\pmod 5\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"powers of 2 are never divisible by 5"},{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{24} \\equiv 1\"></span>, times <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>"},{"h":"2","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^4 = 16 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 5\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{25} = (2^4)^6 \\cdot 2 \\equiv 1^6 \\cdot 2 = 2 \\pmod 5\"></span>"},{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 \\equiv 3\"></span>"},{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^2 \\equiv 4\"></span>"}],"why":"Cycle mod 5 has length 4 (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2, 4, 3, 1\"></span>); <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4\"></span>, so remainder is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Today is <strong>Thursday</strong>. What day of the week will it be <strong>45 days</strong> from today?","opts":[{"h":"Friday","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"45 \\equiv 3 \\pmod 7\"></span>, not 1"},{"h":"Saturday","why":"+2 days"},{"h":"Sunday","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"45 = 6 \\times 7 + 3\"></span>, so 3 days after Thursday is Sunday"},{"h":"Monday","why":"+4 days"},{"h":"Wednesday","why":"-1 day"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"45 \\bmod 7 = 3\"></span>; Thursday + 3 days = Sunday.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(21)_4 + (32)_4\"></span> written in <strong>base 4</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(53)_4\"></span>","why":"digits in base 4 must be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt; 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(103)_4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 2 = 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 3 = 5 = 11_4\"></span> → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(113)_4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(113)_4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9 + 14 = 23_{10} = 1\\cdot 16 + 1\\cdot 4 + 3 = (113)_4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(123)_4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8 + 3 = 27\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(111)_4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"21\"></span>"}],"why":"Units: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1+2=3\"></span>; 4s place: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2+3=5 = 1\\cdot 4 + 1 \\implies (113)_4\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Find the units (last) digit of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^{2026}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2026 \\equiv 2 \\pmod 4\"></span>, so same as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^2\"></span>"},{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^3\"></span> ends in 3"},{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^1\"></span> ends in 7"},{"h":"9","ok":1,"why":"units digits of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^n\"></span> cycle every 4: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7, 9, 3, 1\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2026 \\bmod 4 = 2 \\implies 9\"></span>"},{"h":"5","why":"powers of 7 never end in 5"}],"why":"Mod 10 cycle of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7^n\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(7, 9, 3, 1)\"></span> of length 4; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2026 = 4(506) + 2 \\implies 7^2 = 49\"></span> ends in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"How many <strong>positive divisors</strong> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"180\"></span> have?","opts":[{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"180 = 2^2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^1\"></span>"},{"h":"15","why":"arithmetic error"},{"h":"18","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2+1)(2+1)(1+1) = 3 \\times 3 \\times 2 = 18\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\times 3 \\times 2 = 18\"></span>, not 24"},{"h":"9","why":"missed the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+1\"></span> on exponents"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"180 = 2^2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^1 \\implies (2+1)(2+1)(1+1) = 18\"></span> positive divisors.","tag":"05"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(A, B) = 6\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(A, B) = 180\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A = 30\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"18","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"30 \\times 18 = 540 \\ne 1080\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"30 \\times 24 = 720 \\ne 1080\"></span>"},{"h":"36","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cdot B = 6 \\times 180 = 1080 \\implies B = 1080 / 30 = 36\"></span>"},{"h":"45","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"30 \\times 45 = 1350\"></span>"},{"h":"60","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(30, 60) = 30 \\ne 6\"></span>"}],"why":"Using <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cdot B = \\gcd(A, B) \\cdot \\operatorname{lcm}(A, B)\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"B = (6 \\times 180) / 30 = 36\"></span>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Two alarms beep every 18 seconds and 24 seconds. If they beep together at <code>12:00:00</code>, when do they next beep together?","opts":[{"h":"<code>12:00:42</code>","why":"42 is not divisible by 18 or 24"},{"h":"<code>12:00:48</code>","why":"48 is not divisible by 18"},{"h":"<code>12:01:12</code>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(18, 24) = 72\"></span> seconds = 1 min 12 sec"},{"h":"<code>12:01:36</code>","why":"96 sec is not divisible by 18"},{"h":"<code>12:02:00</code>","why":"120 sec is not divisible by 18"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{lcm}(18, 24) = 72\"></span> seconds after <code>12:00:00</code> is <code>12:01:12</code>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Which pair of numbers is <strong>coprime</strong> (aralarında asal)?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(14, 21)\"></span>","why":"common factor 7"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(15, 25)\"></span>","why":"common factor 5"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(18, 27)\"></span>","why":"common factor 9"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(16, 25)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 = 2^4\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25 = 5^2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(16, 25) = 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(21, 35)\"></span>","why":"common factor 7"}],"why":"Coprime numbers share no prime factors (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd = 1\"></span>): <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25\"></span>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"What is the sum of the two <strong>smallest prime numbers</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 2 = 3\"></span>, but <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span> is NOT prime!"},{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 2\"></span> repeats 2"},{"h":"5","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 3 = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 5\"></span> skips 3"},{"h":"8","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 + 5\"></span> skips 2"}],"why":"The smallest primes are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 + 3 = 5\"></span>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3^4 \\cdot 9^2}{27^2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^8 / 3^6 = 3^2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^4 \\cdot 3^4 / 3^6 = 3^{8-6} = 3^2 = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"27\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"81\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^4\"></span>"}],"why":"Convert 9 and 27 to base 3: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3^4 \\cdot (3^2)^2}{(3^3)^2} = \\frac{3^8}{3^6} = 3^2 = 9\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2)^3 + 2^{-2} \\cdot 8\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-10\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2)^3 = -8\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1/4)\\cdot 8 = +2\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8 + 2 = -6\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-6\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8 + \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 = -8 + 2 = -6\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4\"></span>","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2)^3\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+8\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\"></span>","why":"wrong sign on both terms"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2)^3 = -8\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{-2} \\cdot 8 = \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 8 = 2\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8 + 2 = -6\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^{2x - 1} = 125\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^1 = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"125 = 5^3 \\implies 2x - 1 = 3 \\implies x = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^5 \\ne 125\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","why":"too large"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = \\frac{3}{2}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(3/2) - 1 = 2 \\ne 3\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"125 = 5^3\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 1 = 3 \\implies x = 2\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2^{10} + 2^{10}}{2^9}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\cdot 2^{10} = 2^{11}\"></span>, divided by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^9\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^2 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2 \\cdot 2^{10}}{2^9} = \\frac{2^{11}}{2^9} = 2^2 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{11}\"></span>","why":"forgot to divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{10} + 2^{10} \\ne 2^{20}\"></span>"}],"why":"Factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{10}\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{10}(1 + 1) = 2^{11}\"></span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{11} / 2^9 = 2^2 = 4\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^x = 5\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{x + 2}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\"></span>","why":"added 2 instead of multiplying by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 \\times 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"45\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{x+2} = 3^x \\cdot 3^2 = 5 \\times 9 = 45\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"125\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^3\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{x+2} = 3^x \\cdot 3^2 = 5 \\cdot 9 = 45\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{48} + \\sqrt{27} - \\sqrt{12}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt{3} - 2\\sqrt{3} = 5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt{3} - 2\\sqrt{3} = 5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","why":"forgot to subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{12} = 2\\sqrt{3}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","why":"added all three"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{63}\"></span>","why":"cannot add inside roots"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\\sqrt{3} + 3\\sqrt{3} - 2\\sqrt{3} = 5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Rationalize <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2})\"></span>","why":"wrong sign in numerator"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2})\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"multiply by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2}}\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{6(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2})}{5-2} = 2(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2})\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2})\"></span>","why":"forgot to divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 2 = 3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2}\"></span>","why":"divided by 6 instead of 3"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2})\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6/3 = 2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>"}],"why":"Conjugate gives denominator <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 - 2 = 3\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 / 3 = 2\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 0\"></span>, simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} + x\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x\"></span>","why":"since <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 0\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} = |x| = -x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} = |x| = -x\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-x + x = 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-x + x = 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>","why":"missed <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} \\ne x^2\"></span>"}],"why":"For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 0\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x| = -x\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-x + x = 0\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Compute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{12 + \\sqrt{13 + \\sqrt{9}}}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{12 + 4} = \\sqrt{16} = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"inner <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{9}=3 \\to \\sqrt{16}=4 \\to \\sqrt{12+4} = \\sqrt{16} = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{25}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"too large"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"too small"}],"why":"Work inside-out: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{9}=3\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{13+3}=4\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{12+4}=4\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Write <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[3]{x^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{x}\"></span> as a single power of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; 0\"></span>):","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{1/6}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{7}{6}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{5/6}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{5}{6}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{7/6}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{2/3} \\cdot x^{1/2} = x^{4/6 + 3/6} = x^{7/6}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{3/5}\"></span>","why":"added numerators and denominators"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^{1/3}\"></span>","why":"multiplied exponents"}],"why":"Add fractional exponents: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{7}{6}\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - y = 5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"xy = 6\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + y^2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"13","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25 - 12 = 13\"></span>, wait: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-y)^2 = x^2 - 2xy + y^2 \\implies 25 = x^2+y^2 - 12 \\implies x^2+y^2 = 37\"></span>!"},{"h":"25","why":"forgot <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2xy\"></span>"},{"h":"31","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"xy\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2xy\"></span>"},{"h":"37","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + y^2 = (x - y)^2 + 2xy = 25 + 12 = 37\"></span>"},{"h":"49","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+y)^2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-y)^2 = x^2 - 2xy + y^2 \\implies x^2 + y^2 = 5^2 + 2(6) = 37\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Factor completely: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x^2 - 27\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(x - 9)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3x - 9)(x + 3)\"></span>","why":"factors out another 3"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(x - 3)(x + 3)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"factor 3 first: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(x^2 - 9) = 3(x - 3)(x + 3)\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3(x - 3)^2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-3)^2 = x^2 - 6x + 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 3)(x + 3)\"></span>","why":"lost the factor of 3"}],"why":"Pull out GCF <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>, then apply difference of squares.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x^3 - 8}{x^2 + 2x + 4}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + 2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^3 - 8 = (x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 4)\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"numerator factors as <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 4)\"></span>, canceling the denominator"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 = 2^3\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 2\"></span>","why":"cannot cancel terms across addition"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"not equal"}],"why":"Difference of cubes: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^3 - 2^3 = (x - 2)(x^2 + 2x + 4)\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + \\frac{1}{x} = 4\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"16","why":"forgot to subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"18","why":"added 2 instead of subtracting"},{"h":"14","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + \\frac{1}{x})^2 = x^2 + 2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 \\implies x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 14\"></span>"},{"h":"12","why":"subtracted 4"},{"h":"8","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 2\"></span>"}],"why":"Square both sides: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 \\implies x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 14\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x^2 + 5x - 3\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x + 1)(x - 3)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5x\"></span> in the middle"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 1)(x + 3)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x\\cdot 3 - 1\\cdot x = +5x\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-1)(3) = -3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x + 3)(x - 1)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+x\"></span> in the middle"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 3)(x + 1)\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-x\"></span> in the middle"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + 3)(x - 1)\"></span>","why":"leading coefficient is 1, not 2"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 1)(x + 3) = 2x^2 + 6x - x - 3 = 2x^2 + 5x - 3\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"103^2 - 97^2\"></span> quickly using an identity:","opts":[{"h":"600","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(103-97)(103+97) = 6 \\times 200 = 1200\"></span>"},{"h":"1200","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (103 - 97)(103 + 97) = 6 \\times 200 = 1200\"></span>"},{"h":"36","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(103 - 97)^2\"></span>"},{"h":"200","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"103 + 97\"></span> only"},{"h":"2400","why":"doubled 1200"}],"why":"Difference of squares: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(103 - 97)(103 + 97) = 6 \\times 200 = 1200\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x + 2}{3} - \\frac{x - 1}{2} = 1\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -1\"></span>","why":"check: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1/3 - (-2)/2 = 4/3 \\ne 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 1\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"multiply by 6: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(x+2) - 3(x-1) = 6 \\implies 2x+4-3x+3=6 \\implies -x+7=6 \\implies x=1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>","why":"check: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5/3 - 1 = 2/3 \\ne 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span>","why":"check: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7/3 - 2 = 1/3 \\ne 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -5\"></span>","why":"sign error"}],"why":"Multiply by 6: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x + 4 - 3x + 3 = 6 \\implies 7 - x = 6 \\implies x = 1\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Solve the system: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x + 3y = 13\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - y = 4\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(4, 0)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(4) + 0 = 8 \\ne 13\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(5, 1)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = y + 4 \\implies 2(y+4) + 3y = 13 \\implies 5y = 5 \\implies y = 1, x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3, -1)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(3) - 3 = 3 \\ne 13\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(6, 2)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(6) + 6 = 18 \\ne 13\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1, 5)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 - 5 = -4 \\ne 4\"></span>"}],"why":"Substitute <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = y + 4\"></span> into the first equation: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5y + 8 = 13 \\implies y = 1, x = 5\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"For which <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a - 3)x + 2 = 2x + b\"></span> hold for <strong>all</strong> real <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> (infinitely many solutions) when <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b = 2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2-3)x = -x \\ne 2x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0x = 2x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 5\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"coefficient of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> must match on both sides: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a - 3 = 2 \\implies a = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x \\ne 2x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = -5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8x \\ne 2x\"></span>"}],"why":"For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0x = 0\"></span>, both sides must have the same <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>-coefficient: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a - 3 = 2 \\implies a = 5\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"The sum of three consecutive integers is <code>57</code>. What is the <strong>largest</strong> of the three?","opts":[{"h":"18","why":"18 is the smallest (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18+19+20=57\"></span>)"},{"h":"19","why":"19 is the middle integer"},{"h":"20","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n + (n+1) + (n+2) = 57 \\implies 3n + 3 = 57 \\implies n = 18\"></span>, largest <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 20\"></span>"},{"h":"21","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"19+20+21 = 60\"></span>"},{"h":"22","why":"too large"}],"why":"Middle integer is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"57 / 3 = 19\"></span>, so the integers are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18, 19, 20\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4(x - 2) = 2(x + 6)\"></span>, find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x - 8 = 2x + 12 \\implies 2x = 20 \\implies x = 10\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"8","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"10","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x - 8 = 2x + 12 \\implies 2x = 20 \\implies x = 10\"></span>"},{"h":"12","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x = 24\"></span> would need <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+16\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x - 8 = 2x + 12 \\implies 2x = 20 \\implies x = 10\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"What is the <strong>discriminant</strong> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta\"></span>) of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x^2 - 4x + 5 = 0\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-24\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = (-4)^2 - 4(2)(5) = 16 - 40 = -24\"></span>! Wait—let's mark <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-24\"></span> as <code>*</code>!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-24\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = (-4)^2 - 4(2)(5) = 16 - 40 = -24\"></span> (no real roots)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"24\"></span>","why":"subtracted wrong way"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"56\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 40\"></span> (sign error on <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4ac\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 - 40 \\ne 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-56\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-4)^2 = +16\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-16\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = (-4)^2 - 4(2)(5) = 16 - 40 = -24\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_2\"></span> are the roots of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x^2 + 9x - 12 = 0\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>","why":"forgot minus sign in <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-b/a\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{9}{3} = -3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"c/a = x_1 x_2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-9\"></span>","why":"forgot to divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a = 3\"></span>"}],"why":"By Vieta's formula, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -b/a = -9/3 = -3\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1, x_2\"></span> are the roots of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 6x + 4 = 0\"></span>, find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{x_1} + \\frac{1}{x_2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>","why":"inverted"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x_1 + x_2}{x_1 x_2} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"forgot to divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = +6\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-6\"></span>"}],"why":"Combine fractions: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x_1 + x_2}{x_1 x_2} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Which quadratic equation has roots <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 = 2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_2 = -5\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 3x - 10 = 0\"></span>","why":"sum is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+3\"></span>, should be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 3x - 10 = 0\"></span>)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 3x - 10 = 0\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 2)(x + 5) = x^2 + 3x - 10 = 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 7x + 10 = 0\"></span>","why":"roots <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 7x + 10 = 0\"></span>","why":"roots <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 3x + 10 = 0\"></span>","why":"product is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-10\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+10\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 2)(x + 5) = x^2 + 3x - 10 = 0\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"For what positive value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"k\"></span> does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + kx + 16 = 0\"></span> have <strong>one repeated real root</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 16 - 64 &lt; 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = k^2 - 64 = 0 \\implies k = 8\"></span> (positive)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 256 - 64 &gt; 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta &lt; 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32\"></span>","why":"too large"}],"why":"Repeated root requires <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = k^2 - 4(1)(16) = 0 \\implies k = 8\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 2x &gt; 13\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; -3\"></span>","why":"forgot to flip <code>&gt;</code> when dividing by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; -3\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x &gt; 6 \\implies x &lt; -3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 3\"></span>","why":"sign error"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; 3\"></span>","why":"both sign and flip errors"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le -3\"></span>","why":"original inequality is strict <code>&gt;</code>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x &gt; 6\"></span>, divide by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span> and flip sign: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; -3\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Find the solution set of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + 2)(x - 5) \\le 0\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -2] \\cup [5, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"that is where the product is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2, 5)\"></span>","why":"strict <code>&lt;</code> excludes endpoints"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-2, 5]\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"roots are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>; expression is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le 0\"></span> between them"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[2, 5]\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-5, 2]\"></span>","why":"swapped signs of roots"}],"why":"Leading coefficient is positive, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+2)(x-5) \\le 0\"></span> holds on <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-2, 5]\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{x + 1}{x - 3} \\ge 0\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -1] \\cup [3, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span> makes the denominator zero (must be excluded!)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -1] \\cup (3, \\infty)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"include <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1\"></span> (numerator root), exclude <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span> (denominator root)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-1, 3)\"></span>","why":"that is where the fraction is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-1, 3)\"></span>","why":"wrong sign and excluded <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"missed <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -1]\"></span>"}],"why":"Positive outside <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-1, 3)\"></span>; include <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1\"></span>, exclude <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -1] \\cup (3, \\infty)\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"How many integers satisfy <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-4 &lt; 2x \\le 6\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"4","why":"missed an endpoint"},{"h":"5","ok":1,"why":"divide by 2: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2 &lt; x \\le 3\"></span>, integers <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{-1, 0, 1, 2, 3\\}\"></span> (5 integers)"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span> is excluded by strict <code>&lt;</code>"},{"h":"3","why":"missed negatives/zero"},{"h":"7","why":"too many"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2 &lt; x \\le 3\"></span> contains <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-1, 0, 1, 2, 3\"></span> — 5 integers.","tag":"11"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3 &lt; x &lt; 4\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 &lt; y &lt; 5\"></span>, what is the <strong>integer maximum</strong> of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"7","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y &lt; 4 + 5 = 9\"></span>, so largest integer is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>"},{"h":"8","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y &lt; 9\"></span>, so maximum integer is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>"},{"h":"9","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span> is excluded because both inequalities are strict <code>&lt;</code>"},{"h":"6","why":"too small"},{"h":"10","why":"impossible"}],"why":"Adding strict inequalities gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y &lt; 9\"></span>, so the largest integer is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 3| = 7\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 10\"></span> only","why":"missed the negative branch <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 3 = -7\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -4\"></span>","why":"forgot the <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3\"></span> shift"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 10\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 3 = 7 \\implies 10\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 3 = -7 \\implies -4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -10\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","why":"swapped signs"},{"h":"No solution","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 &gt; 0\"></span>, so 2 solutions exist"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 3 = \\pm 7\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 10\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -4\"></span>.","tag":"12"},{"q":"What is the solution set of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|2x + 1| = -5\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{-3, 2\\}\"></span>","why":"checked without noticing RHS is negative"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{-3\\}\"></span>","why":"distance cannot be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{2\\}\"></span>","why":"distance cannot be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\"></span> (no solution)","ok":1,"why":"an absolute value is always <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 0\"></span> and can never equal <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span>","why":"false"}],"why":"Absolute value is never negative, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|2x + 1| = -5\"></span> has no solution.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x + 2| &lt; 5\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-3, 7)\"></span>","why":"shifted wrong direction"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-7, 3)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5 &lt; x + 2 &lt; 5 \\implies -7 &lt; x &lt; 3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-7, 3]\"></span>","why":"strict <code>&lt;</code> gives open interval"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -7) \\cup (3, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x + 2| &gt; 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-5, 5)\"></span>","why":"forgot <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5 &lt; x + 2 &lt; 5 \\implies -7 &lt; x &lt; 3\"></span>.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Find the <strong>minimum</strong> possible value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 4| + 3\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 4| \\ge 0\"></span>, so adding <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>","why":"too small"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"minimum occurs when <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>, giving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 + 3 = 3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\"></span>","why":"occurs at <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>"}],"why":"Since <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 4| \\ge 0\"></span>, the smallest value is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0 + 3 = 3\"></span> (at <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>).","tag":"12"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 &lt; x &lt; 5\"></span>, simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 1| + |x - 6|\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x - 7\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 6 &lt; 0\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 6| = 6 - x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 1) + (6 - x) = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 + 1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x + 5\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span> cancels out"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-5\"></span>","why":"sum of absolute values is positive"}],"why":"On <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1, 5)\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 1 &gt; 0\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - 6 &lt; 0\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x - 1) + (6 - x) = 5\"></span>.","tag":"12"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a : b = 3 : 4\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b = 35\"></span>, find <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"15","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a\"></span>"},{"h":"20","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3k + 4k = 35 \\implies k = 5 \\implies b = 4(5) = 20\"></span>"},{"h":"21","why":"arithmetic error"},{"h":"25","why":"arithmetic error"},{"h":"28","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 7\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7k = 35 \\implies k = 5\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b = 4 \\times 5 = 20\"></span>.","tag":"13"},{"q":"8 machines produce a batch of parts in 15 hours. How many hours will 10 identical machines take?","opts":[{"h":"10 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 \\times 15 = 120 \\ne 100\"></span>"},{"h":"12 hours","ok":1,"why":"inverse proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 \\times 15 = 10 \\times t \\implies t = 120 / 10 = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"18.75 hours","why":"used direct proportion (more machines should take LESS time!)"},{"h":"13 hours","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"14 hours","why":"arithmetic slip"}],"why":"Inverse proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 \\cdot 15 = 10 \\cdot t \\implies t = 12\"></span> hours.","tag":"13"},{"q":"A laptop priced at <code>20,000 TL</code> gets a <strong>15% discount</strong>. What is the sale price?","opts":[{"h":"<code>15,000 TL</code>","why":"that is a 25% discount"},{"h":"<code>16,500 TL</code>","why":"that is 17.5% off"},{"h":"<code>17,000 TL</code>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20000 \\times 0.85 = 17000\"></span> TL (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15\\% = 3000\"></span> TL off)"},{"h":"<code>18,500 TL</code>","why":"7.5% off"},{"h":"<code>19,000 TL</code>","why":"5% off"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15\\%\"></span> of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20000\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3000\"></span>, leaving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"17000\"></span> TL.","tag":"13"},{"q":"A shop raises a price by <strong>10%</strong> and later cuts the new price by <strong>10%</strong>. Compared to the original price, the final price is:","opts":[{"h":"Equal to the original price","why":"percentages apply to different bases"},{"h":"1% higher","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+10\\%\"></span> then <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-10\\%\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1.10 \\times 0.90 = 0.99\"></span>"},{"h":"1% lower","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1.10 \\times 0.90 = 0.99\"></span> (a 1% decrease)"},{"h":"2% lower","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10\\% \\times 10\\% = 1\\%\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\\%\"></span>"},{"h":"10% lower","why":"too much"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100 \\to 110 \\to 99\"></span>: a net <strong>1% decrease</strong>.","tag":"13"},{"q":"40 grams of salt are dissolved in 160 grams of water. What is the <strong>salt percentage</strong> of the mixture?","opts":[{"h":"25%","why":"divided <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"40 / 160\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"40 / (40 + 160)\"></span>"},{"h":"20%","ok":1,"why":"total weight <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 40 + 160 = 200\"></span> g; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"40 / 200 = 20\\%\"></span>"},{"h":"16%","why":"incorrect"},{"h":"40%","why":"40 g out of 200 g, not 100 g"},{"h":"22.5%","why":"incorrect"}],"why":"Salt percentage <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= \\frac{\\text{salt}}{\\text{total mixture}} = \\frac{40}{40 + 160} = \\frac{40}{200} = 20\\%\"></span>.","tag":"13"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A) = 8\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(B) = 6\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B = \\emptyset\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"2","why":"subtracted instead of adding"},{"h":"10","why":"no overlap to subtract"},{"h":"14","ok":1,"why":"disjoint sets have <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cap B) = 0\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8 + 6 = 14\"></span>"},{"h":"48","why":"multiplied"},{"h":"7","why":"incorrect"}],"why":"Disjoint sets (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"A \\cap B = \\emptyset\"></span>) satisfy <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = s(A) + s(B) = 14\"></span>.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{3}{10} - \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{10}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4 + 3 - 5}{10} = \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{5}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4}{10} + \\frac{3}{10} - \\frac{5}{10} = \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{3}{5}\"></span>","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span> instead of subtracting"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{5}\"></span>","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4+3-5 = 2 \\ne 0\"></span>"}],"why":"Common denominator 10 gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{4 + 3 - 5}{10} = \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5}\"></span>.","tag":"02"},{"q":"What is the remainder when <code>123456</code> is divided by <strong>3</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"0","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1+2+3+4+5+6 = 21\"></span>, which is divisible by 3"},{"h":"1","why":"sum is 21"},{"h":"2","why":"sum is 21"},{"h":"3","why":"remainder mod 3 must be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt; 3\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"remainder mod 3 must be <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt; 3\"></span>"}],"why":"Digit sum is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"21 = 3 \\times 7\"></span>, so remainder is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Find the largest possible value of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span> if the 4-digit number <code>2a4b</code> is divisible by <strong>15</strong>:","opts":[{"h":"9","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=0, a=9 \\implies 9\"></span>"},{"h":"10","why":"larger exists"},{"h":"12","ok":1,"why":"for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=5\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2+a+4+5 = 11+a\"></span> is div by 3 when <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=7\"></span>, giving <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7+5=12\"></span>"},{"h":"14","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=9, b=5\"></span> gives sum <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20\"></span> (not div by 3)"},{"h":"15","why":"impossible"}],"why":"Checking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=5\"></span> gives max <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=7\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b=12\"></span>); checking <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b=0\"></span> gives max <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a=9\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b=9\"></span>). Largest <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a+b\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12\"></span>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Convert <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(11101)_2\"></span> to decimal:","opts":[{"h":"25","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16+8+1\"></span>"},{"h":"27","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16+8+2+1\"></span>"},{"h":"29","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8 + 4 + 0 + 1 = 29\"></span>"},{"h":"30","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16+8+4+2\"></span>"},{"h":"31","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"11111_2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16 + 8 + 4 + 1 = 29\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"123 \\bmod 7\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"2","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 \\times 17 = 119\"></span>"},{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"123 - 119 = 4\"></span>"},{"h":"4","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"123 = 7 \\times 17 + 4\"></span>"},{"h":"5","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"124 \\bmod 7 = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"125 \\bmod 7 = 6\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 \\times 17 = 119\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"123 - 119 = 4\"></span>.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(45, 75)\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"5","why":"15 is larger"},{"h":"9","why":"9 does not divide 75"},{"h":"15","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"45 = 3^2 \\cdot 5\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"75 = 3 \\cdot 5^2 \\implies \\gcd = 3 \\cdot 5 = 15\"></span>"},{"h":"25","why":"25 does not divide 45"},{"h":"225","why":"225 is the LCM, not GCD"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(45, 75) = 15\"></span>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^{-1/2}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>","why":"negative exponent means reciprocal, not negative sign"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","why":"positive base stays positive"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^{-1/2} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","why":"forgot the minus sign in the exponent"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{1}{16}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^{-2} = 1/16\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4^{-1/2} = \\frac{1}{4^{1/2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{18} \\cdot \\sqrt{8}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{144} = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","why":"too small"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{18 \\cdot 8} = \\sqrt{144} = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{256}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"24\"></span>","why":"doubled"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{18} \\cdot \\sqrt{8} = \\sqrt{144} = 12\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Expand <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3x - 2)^2\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9x^2 - 4\"></span>","why":"forgot the middle term <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-12x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9x^2 + 4\"></span>","why":"forgot <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-12x\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9x^2 - 6x + 4\"></span>","why":"forgot to double <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x \\cdot 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9x^2 - 12x + 4\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3x)^2 - 2(3x)(2) + 2^2 = 9x^2 - 12x + 4\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x^2 - 12x + 4\"></span>","why":"forgot to square <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a-b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2 = 9x^2 - 12x + 4\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x^2 - 49\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 7)^2\"></span>","why":"gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-28x\"></span> middle term"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 7)(2x + 7)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"difference of squares <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x)^2 - 7^2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(4x - 7)(x + 7)\"></span>","why":"wrong coefficients"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4(x - 7)(x + 7)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4 \\times 49 \\ne 49\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(2x - 49)(2x + 1)\"></span>","why":"wrong constants"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4x^2 - 49 = (2x)^2 - 7^2 = (2x - 7)(2x + 7)\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5x - 3 = 2x + 12\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x = 15 \\implies x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 4\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20 - 3 \\ne 8 + 12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x = 15 \\implies x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 6\"></span>","why":"too large"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 9\"></span>","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\"></span> wrong"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5x - 2x = 12 + 3 \\implies 3x = 15 \\implies x = 5\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + y = 10\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x - y = 4\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - y^2\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"14","why":"added <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10 + 4\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"40","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) = 10 \\times 4 = 40\"></span>"},{"h":"52","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x=7, y=3 \\implies 49 - 9 = 40\"></span>"},{"h":"100","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"10^2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x + y)(x - y) = 10 \\cdot 4 = 40\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"How many real roots does <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 4x + 5 = 0\"></span> have?","opts":[{"h":"0","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = 4^2 - 4(1)(5) = 16 - 20 = -4 &lt; 0\"></span> (no real roots)"},{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta \\ne 0\"></span>"},{"h":"2","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta &lt; 0\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&gt; 0\"></span>"},{"h":"3","why":"quadratic has at most 2 roots"},{"h":"Infinitely many","why":"non-zero polynomial"}],"why":"Since <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = -4 &lt; 0\"></span>, there are <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span> real roots.","tag":"10"},{"q":"For <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 8x + 12 = 0\"></span>, what is the <strong>product</strong> of the roots?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-8\"></span> is the negative sum"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"8\"></span> is the sum of roots"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = c/a = 12/1 = 12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-12\"></span>","why":"sign is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+12\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span> is one root (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6\"></span>), not the product"}],"why":"By Vieta, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = c/a = 12\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x - 4 \\le 2x + 5\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le 1\"></span>","why":"added 4 to both sides: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + 4 = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le 9\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x - 2x \\le 5 + 4 \\implies x \\le 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ge 9\"></span>","why":"did not divide by a negative, so sign does not flip"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 9\"></span>","why":"original is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt;\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le -1\"></span>","why":"sign error"}],"why":"Subtract <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x\"></span> and add <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\le 9\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Which interval represents <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\{x \\in \\mathbb{R} : -2 \\le x &lt; 5\\}\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2, 5)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span> should be included <code>[</code>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-2, 5)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<code>-2</code> closed <code>[</code>, <code>5</code> open <code>)</code>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-2, 5]\"></span>","why":"endpoints swapped"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-2, 5]\"></span>","why":"<code>5</code> should be excluded <code>)</code>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, 5)\"></span>","why":"missed lower bound <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>"}],"why":"Closed bracket <code>[</code> for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le\"></span> and open parenthesis <code>)</code> for <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt;\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-2, 5)\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|3x - 6| \\le 9\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-1, 5]\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-9 \\le 3x - 6 \\le 9 \\implies -3 \\le 3x \\le 15 \\implies -1 \\le x \\le 5\"></span>!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-1, 5]\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-9 \\le 3x - 6 \\le 9 \\implies -3 \\le 3x \\le 15 \\implies [-1, 5]\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-1, 5)\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\le\"></span> includes endpoints"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[1, 5]\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3 / 3 = -1\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"+1\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"[-5, 1]\"></span>","why":"wrong signs"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(-\\infty, -1] \\cup [5, \\infty)\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 9\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-9 \\le 3x - 6 \\le 9 \\implies -3 \\le 3x \\le 15 \\implies [-1, 5]\"></span>.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|-7| - |3 - 10| + |-2|\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-12\"></span>","why":"each absolute value is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\ge 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 7 + 2 = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 7 + 2 = 2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"16\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 + 7 + 2\"></span> (missed minus sign between terms)"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 7 + 2 = +2\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|-7| = 7\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|3 - 10| = |-7| = 7\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|-2| = 2\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 - 7 + 2 = 2\"></span>.","tag":"12"},{"q":"A car travels at <code>80 km/h</code> and takes <code>3 hours</code> for a trip. How long will the same trip take at <code>60 km/h</code>?","opts":[{"h":"2.25 hours","why":"used direct proportion"},{"h":"3.5 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"60 \\times 3.5 = 210 \\ne 240\"></span>"},{"h":"4 hours","ok":1,"why":"distance <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 80 \\times 3 = 240\"></span> km; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"240 / 60 = 4\"></span> hours"},{"h":"4.5 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"60 \\times 4.5 = 270\"></span>"},{"h":"5 hours","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"60 \\times 5 = 300\"></span>"}],"why":"Speed and time are inversely proportional: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"80 \\times 3 = 60 \\times t \\implies t = 4\"></span> hours.","tag":"13"},{"q":"What is <strong>30%</strong> of <strong>250</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"50","why":"20% of 250"},{"h":"65","why":"arithmetic slip"},{"h":"75","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"250 \\times 0.30 = 75\"></span>"},{"h":"80","why":"32% of 250"},{"h":"85","why":"arithmetic slip"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.30 \\times 250 = 75\"></span>.","tag":"13"},{"q":"A class has 18 boys and 12 girls. What <strong>percentage</strong> of the class are <strong>girls</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"12%","why":"12 is the count, not the percentage out of 30"},{"h":"30%","why":"30 is total students"},{"h":"40%","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 / (18 + 12) = 12 / 30 = 0.40 = 40\\%\"></span>"},{"h":"60%","why":"60% are boys"},{"h":"66.7%","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 / 18\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 / 30\"></span>"}],"why":"Total students <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 18 + 12 = 30\"></span>; girls <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= \\frac{12}{30} = 40\\%\"></span>.","tag":"13"},{"q":"Which of the following numbers is <strong>prime</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"1","why":"1 is not prime"},{"h":"21","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\times 7\"></span>"},{"h":"27","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^3\"></span>"},{"h":"29","ok":1,"why":"only divisible by 1 and 29"},{"h":"39","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 \\times 13\"></span>"}],"why":"29 has no divisors other than 1 and 29.","tag":"05"},{"q":"What is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^0 + 3^0 + 4^0\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"0","why":"any nonzero number to the 0th power is 1"},{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 1 + 1 = 3\"></span>"},{"h":"3","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 1 + 1 = 3\"></span>"},{"h":"9","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2+3+4 = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"24","why":"multiplied"}],"why":"Each term equals <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 + 1 + 1 = 3\"></span>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{75}\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{45}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{25 \\cdot 3} = 5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"15\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"too large"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"25\\sqrt{3}\"></span>","why":"forgot to take square root of 25"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5\\sqrt{5}\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{125}\"></span>"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{75} = \\sqrt{25 \\cdot 3} = 5\\sqrt{3}\"></span>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = 35\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a - b = 5\"></span>, what is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"5","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"35 / 5 = 7\"></span>"},{"h":"7","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a - b)(a + b) = 35 \\implies 5(a + b) = 35 \\implies a + b = 7\"></span>"},{"h":"30","why":"subtracted instead of dividing"},{"h":"40","why":"added"},{"h":"175","why":"multiplied"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a + b = 35 / 5 = 7\"></span>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{2}{x} = \\frac{6}{15}\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\ne 0\"></span>):","opts":[{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 3 = 18 \\ne 30\"></span>"},{"h":"4","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 4 = 24 \\ne 30\"></span>"},{"h":"5","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x = 30 \\implies x = 5\"></span>"},{"h":"6","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6 \\times 6 = 36 \\ne 30\"></span>"},{"h":"10","why":"doubled"}],"why":"Cross-multiply: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x = 2 \\cdot 15 = 30 \\implies x = 5\"></span>.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 9x = 0\"></span>:","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 9\"></span> only","why":"lost <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span> by dividing by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>!"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span> only","why":"missed <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 9\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"factor: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x(x - 9) = 0 \\implies x = 0\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 9\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 3\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -3\"></span>","why":"that is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 9 = 0\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -9\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x + 9 = 0\"></span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-9\"></span>"}],"why":"Never divide both sides by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x\"></span>; factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x(x - 9) = 0\"></span> to keep <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 0\"></span>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Which integer is in the solution set of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x + 1 &gt; 7\"></span>?","opts":[{"h":"1","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3 &gt; 7\"></span> is false"},{"h":"2","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 &gt; 7\"></span> is false"},{"h":"3","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"7 &gt; 7\"></span> is false (strict <code>&gt;</code>)"},{"h":"4","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2(4) + 1 = 9 &gt; 7\"></span> is true (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; 3\"></span>)"},{"h":"0","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"1 &gt; 7\"></span> is false"}],"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2x &gt; 6 \\implies x &gt; 3\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"4\"></span> is the only option <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&gt; 3\"></span>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"An item's price increases from <code>80 TL</code> to <code>100 TL</code>. What is the <strong>percentage increase</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"20%","why":"divided <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"20\"></span> by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"100\"></span> (new) instead of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"80\"></span> (old)"},{"h":"25%","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{100 - 80}{80} = \\frac{20}{80} = 25\\%\"></span>"},{"h":"15%","why":"incorrect"},{"h":"30%","why":"incorrect"},{"h":"80%","why":"incorrect"}],"why":"Percentage change <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= \\frac{\\text{new} - \\text{old}}{\\text{old}} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{20}{80} = 25\\%\"></span>.","tag":"13"}],"exercises":[],"challenges":[],"cheat":{"html":"<section class=\"sec sec-1-sets-primes-gcd-lcm\"><h2 id=\"1-sets-primes-gcd-lcm\">1. Sets, primes, GCD &amp; LCM</h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"s(A \\cup B) = s(A) + s(B) - s(A \\cap B)\"></span> · Subsets of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"n\"></span>-element set: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^n\"></span>.</li><li>If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"N = p_1^{a} p_2^{b} \\cdots\"></span>, positive divisors <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= (a+1)(b+1)\\cdots\"></span></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\gcd(A, B) \\times \\operatorname{lcm}(A, B) = A \\times B\"></span></li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-2-divisibility-repeating-decimals\"><h2 id=\"2-divisibility-repeating-decimals\">2. Divisibility &amp; repeating decimals</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>3 / 9</strong>: digit sum divisible by 3 / 9 · <strong>4</strong>: last 2 digits · <strong>8</strong>: last 3 digits · <strong>11</strong>: alternating sum (<code>+ - + -</code>).</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.\\overline{a} = \\frac{a}{9}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"0.a\\overline{b} = \\frac{ab - a}{90}\"></span></li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-3-exponents-radicals\"><h2 id=\"3-exponents-radicals\">3. Exponents &amp; radicals</h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^m a^n = a^{m+n}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\frac{a^m}{a^n} = a^{m-n}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a^m)^n = a^{mn}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^0 = 1\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a \\ne 0\"></span>)</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt[n]{a^m} = a^{m/n}\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\"></span> · Conjugate of <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b}\"></span>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-4-identities-quadratics\"><h2 id=\"4-identities-quadratics\">4. Identities &amp; quadratics</h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a \\pm b)^2 = a^2 \\pm 2ab + b^2\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)\"></span></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^3 \\pm b^3 = (a \\pm b)(a^2 \\mp ab + b^2)\"></span></li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax^2 + bx + c = 0\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_{1,2} = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a}\"></span></li><li><strong>Vieta</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{b}{a}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x_1 x_2 = \\frac{c}{a}\"></span></li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-5-inequalities-absolute-value-proportion\"><h2 id=\"5-inequalities-absolute-value-proportion\">5. Inequalities, absolute value &amp; proportion</h2>\n<ul><li>Dividing by a negative <strong>flips</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt;, &gt;, \\le, \\ge\"></span>. Never include denominator roots!</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| &lt; a \\iff -a &lt; u &lt; a\"></span> · <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|u| &gt; a \\iff u &lt; -a \\text{ or } u &gt; a\"></span></li><li>Direct proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"y/x = k\"></span> · Inverse proportion: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x \\cdot y = k\"></span></li></ul>\n</section>","title":"Mathematics I — Cheat Sheet"},"mocks":{},"extra":{},"essentials":{"html":"<p>This is <strong>high-school basic maths, not calculus</strong>. The exam is multiple choice, so what matters is knowing the few rules that unlock each question type. Six ideas cover most of it.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Kinds of numbers and divisibility</div><p><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N}\"></span> natural (0, 1, 2…) ⊂ <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Z}\"></span> integers (… −1, 0, 1 …) ⊂ <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Q}\"></span> fractions ⊂ <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"></span> real numbers. Numbers like <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\pi\"></span> are <strong>irrational</strong>.</p>\n<p>Quick divisibility tests: <strong>2</strong> last digit even · <strong>3</strong> digit sum divisible by 3 · <strong>4</strong> last two digits · <strong>5</strong> ends in 0 or 5 · <strong>9</strong> digit sum divisible by 9 · <strong>10</strong> ends in 0.</p>\n<p>Example: 4,512 → digit sum 12 → divisible by 3, not by 9.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-03\">Go deeper: divisibility</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">GCD and LCM</div><p>Break numbers into <strong>prime factors</strong>. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"12 = 2^2 \\cdot 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"18 = 2 \\cdot 3^2\"></span>.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>GCD</strong> (EBOB) = common primes, <strong>smallest</strong> powers: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2 \\cdot 3 = 6\"></span>.</li><li><strong>LCM</strong> (EKOK) = all primes, <strong>largest</strong> powers: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^2 \\cdot 3^2 = 36\"></span>.</li></ul>\n<p>GCD questions sound like \"cut into <strong>equal pieces</strong>, as <strong>large</strong> as possible\". LCM questions sound like \"when do they <strong>meet again</strong>?\"</p>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-05\">Go deeper: GCD and LCM</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Exponents and roots</div><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^m \\cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^3 \\cdot 2^4 = 2^7\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^m / a^n = a^{m-n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5^6 / 5^4 = 5^2\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(a^m)^n = a^{mn}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(3^2)^3 = 3^6\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^0 = 1\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{-3} = \\frac{1}{8}\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{a \\cdot b} = \\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{50} = 5\\sqrt{2}\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Same base → add/subtract the exponents. To solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^{x} = 32\"></span>, write <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"32 = 2^5\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = 5\"></span>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-06\">Go deeper: exponents</a> · <a href=\"#/lesson/math-07\">radicals</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Factoring: three patterns</div><ul><li><strong>Take out what's common:</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"6x + 9 = 3(2x + 3)\"></span></li><li><strong>Difference of squares:</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)\"></span> → <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 25 = (x-5)(x+5)\"></span></li><li><strong>Trinomial:</strong> find two numbers that <strong>multiply</strong> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"c\"></span> and <strong>add</strong> to <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 + 5x + 6 = (x+2)(x+3)\"></span></li></ul>\n<p>Factoring is the key to simplifying fractions and solving quadratics.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-08\">Go deeper: factoring</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Solving equations and inequalities</div><ul><li><strong>Linear:</strong> do the same thing to both sides. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3x + 4 = 19 \\Rightarrow 3x = 15 \\Rightarrow x = 5\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Quadratic</strong> <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"ax^2 + bx + c = 0\"></span>: factor, or use <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a}\"></span> with <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac\"></span>. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta &gt; 0\"></span> two roots, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= 0\"></span> one, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"&lt; 0\"></span> none. Sum of roots <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= -b/a\"></span>, product <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"= c/a\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Inequalities:</strong> like equations, <strong>but multiplying or dividing by a negative flips the sign</strong>: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2x &gt; 6 \\Rightarrow x &lt; -3\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Absolute value</strong> = distance from 0: <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"|x - 3| = 5 \\Rightarrow x = 8\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x = -2\"></span>.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-10\">Go deeper: quadratics</a> · <a href=\"#/lesson/math-11\">inequalities</a> · <a href=\"#/lesson/math-12\">absolute value</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-idea\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Ratio and percentages</div><ul><li><strong>Percent of:</strong> 20% of 150 = <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"150 \\cdot 0.20 = 30\"></span>.</li><li><strong>Increase / decrease by p%:</strong> multiply by <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1 + p/100)\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(1 - p/100)\"></span>. 200 TL + 15% = <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"200 \\cdot 1.15 = 230\"></span> TL.</li><li><strong>Profit %</strong> is always calculated on the <strong>cost</strong> price.</li><li><strong>Direct proportion:</strong> more → more (price of 3 books vs 6 books). <strong>Inverse:</strong> more → less (more workers → fewer days; workers × days stays the same).</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"#/lesson/math-13\">Go deeper: ratio and percentages</a></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-remember\"><div class=\"callout-h\">If you remember only this</div><ul><li>Divisibility by 3 and 9: add the digits.</li><li>GCD = smallest powers (equal pieces); LCM = largest powers (meeting again).</li><li>Same base: multiply → add exponents. <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^0 = 1\"></span>, negative exponent = fraction.</li><li><span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)\"></span>; <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac\"></span>.</li><li>Multiply/divide an inequality by a negative → flip the sign.</li></ul></div>\n<p>Practise with the <a href=\"#/tool/math-mixed\">random question generator</a> — it never runs out and shows every step.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Which number is divisible by 9?","opts":[{"h":"1,234","why":"digit sum 10"},{"h":"4,527","ok":1,"why":"digit sum 18"},{"h":"5,000","why":"digit sum 5"},{"h":"7,771","why":"digit sum 22"}],"why":"Digit sum divisible by 9 → number divisible by 9."},{"q":"What is the LCM of 4 and 6?","opts":[{"h":"2","why":"that's the GCD"},{"h":"24","why":"a common multiple, but not the smallest"},{"h":"12","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"2^2 \\cdot 3\"></span>"},{"h":"10","why":"not a multiple of 4"}],"why":"LCM = smallest number both divide into."},{"q":"Simplify <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^5 \\cdot 3^{-2}\"></span>.","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{-10}\"></span>","why":"multiply → add the exponents, don't multiply them"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"27\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^{5-2} = 3^3\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"9\"></span>","why":"that's <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^2\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"3^7\"></span>","why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"5 + (-2) = 3\"></span>"}],"why":"Add exponents when multiplying the same base."},{"q":"Factor <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x^2 - 7x + 10\"></span>.","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-2)(x-5)\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2 \\cdot -5 = 10\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-2 + (-5) = -7\"></span>"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x+2)(x+5)\"></span>","why":"the sum would be +7"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-1)(x-10)\"></span>","why":"the sum would be −11"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"(x-2)(x+5)\"></span>","why":"the product would be −10"}],"why":"Product <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"c\"></span>, sum <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"b\"></span>."},{"q":"Solve <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x + 1 &gt; 7\"></span>.","opts":[{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; -2\"></span>","why":"the sign must flip when dividing by −3"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; -2\"></span>","ok":1,"why":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"-3x &gt; 6\"></span>, divide by −3 and flip"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &gt; 2\"></span>","why":"wrong sign and value"},{"h":"<span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"x &lt; 2\"></span>","why":"wrong value"}],"why":"Dividing by a negative flips the inequality."}]],"title":"Mathematics I — the essentials","minutes":25,"intro":"numbers, divisibility, exponents and roots, factoring, equations, percentages"}});
